---What OVHcloud offers of the AI Endpoints provider preset: whether the preset can be selected at all, whether its authentication can be provisioned for the agent, the base URL to list available models from, and the model used when the caller states none.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAIEndpointsPreset
---@field apiBase? string OpenAI-compatible base URL, published so a client can list models from its /models sub-path
---@field defaultModel? string|distilled.Null Model seeded when the caller states none. Empty when this deployment states no default
---@field enabled? boolean Whether the OVHcloud AI Endpoints provider preset is available on this deployment
---@field integratedAuth? boolean Whether OVHcloud provisions the AI Endpoints credential for the agent, so the caller does not have to supply one

---A managed AI agent
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgent
---@field createdAt? string Date of the AI agent creation
---@field currentState? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentCurrentState|distilled.Null Current state of the AI agent
---@field id? string Unique identifier of the AI agent
---@field resourceStatus? ovh.cloud_v2.CommonResourceStatusEnum Reflects the readiness of the AI agent: READY, SUSPENDED when it is paused, or DELETING on the response to its deletion
---@field targetSpec? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentTargetSpec Last target specification of the AI agent
---@field updatedAt? string Date of the last AI agent update

---The agent's identity settings, such as its display name.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentConfig
---@field name? string|distilled.Null Display name for the agent, shown in the interface. Empty falls back to a generic label.

---Desired specification of the AI agent to create.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentCreationTargetSpec
---@field config? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsConfig|distilled.Null Optional AI agent configuration seeded at creation, combinable with or used instead of template. Set only here, at creation time; read and changed afterward through the AI agent itself, not through this resource.
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Desired running state of the AI agent. When false the agent is created paused. Defaults to true
---@field name string Name of the AI agent, at most 192 bytes of UTF-8, free of control characters. Unique among this project's agents, with one exception: an agent created before this API enforced uniqueness may share its name with a newer one. Can be changed afterwards through the update endpoint
---@field template? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentTemplateRef|distilled.Null Reference to a template used to seed the AI agent configuration once, at creation time

---Current state of the AI agent
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentCurrentState
---@field aiEndpoints? boolean|distilled.Null Whether this AI agent carries the OVHcloud AI Endpoints provider preset
---@field aiEndpointsIntegratedAuth? boolean|distilled.Null Whether OVHcloud provisioned the AI Endpoints credential for this agent, so the caller did not have to supply one
---@field enabled? boolean Actual running state of the AI agent. False when the agent is paused
---@field endpointUrl? string|distilled.Null URL to invoke the AI agent
---@field name? string Name of the AI agent

---A single delegated sub-persona: either based on a built-in template or defined entirely inline.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentSeed
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Short summary of what this sub-persona is for.
---@field from? string|distilled.Null Optional reference to a built-in template this sub-persona is based on, for example 'builtin:planner'. Any fields set below override the template's defaults.
---@field maxTurns? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of conversational turns this sub-persona may take before returning control. Unset means no cap.
---@field model? string|distilled.Null Model identifier this sub-persona uses when delegated to. Unset reuses the parent agent's model.
---@field soul? string|distilled.Null Persona text and system prompt this sub-persona follows when delegated to.
---@field tools? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentSeedToolsList|distilled.Null Names of the tools this sub-persona is allowed to use.

---Names of the tools this sub-persona is allowed to use.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentSeedToolsList string[]

---Last target specification of the AI agent
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentTargetSpec
---@field enabled? boolean Desired running state of the AI agent. False when the agent is paused
---@field name? string Name of the AI agent

---Reference to a template used to seed the AI agent configuration once, at creation time
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentTemplateRef
---@field id string Identifier of the template to seed the AI agent configuration from. Honored only at creation time

---An issued AI agent access token
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentToken
---@field expiresAt? string|distilled.Null Expiration date of the token. Null when the token does not expire
---@field role? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentTokenRoleEnum Role granted to the token
---@field token? string Bearer token used to authenticate against the AI agent. Returned only once, at mint time

---Role granted to a minted AI agent access token
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentTokenRoleEnum "ADMIN"|"OPERATOR"|"USER"|"VIEWER"

---Desired specification to reconcile the AI agent toward.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentUpdateTargetSpec
---@field enabled boolean Desired running state of the AI agent. Set to false to pause it, true to resume it
---@field name? string|distilled.Null New name for the AI agent, at most 192 bytes of UTF-8, free of control characters. Omitted or null leaves the current name untouched, and so does restating the name the agent already has. Rejected if another agent in this project already has it, with the same exception as at creation. Renaming redeploys the agent on its current runtime component

---Specialized sub-personas this agent can delegate tasks to.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentsConfig
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Master switch for the delegated-agents feature. When false, this agent cannot delegate to a named sub-persona.
---@field items? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentsConfigItemsMap|distilled.Null Sub-personas defined directly in this configuration, keyed by name.

---Sub-personas defined directly in this configuration, keyed by name.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentsConfigItemsMap { [string]: ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentSeed }

---Authentication settings for the agent's HTTP API. Unset falls back to requiring a token issued by the agent itself.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAuthConfig
---@field kagentJwt? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsKagentJwtConfig|distilled.Null Settings for tokens the agent issues and validates itself. Unset or disabled means the agent does not accept self-issued tokens.
---@field mode? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAuthModeEnum|string|distilled.Null Which authentication mode is enforced on the agent's HTTP API.
---@field oauth2? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsOAuth2Config|distilled.Null External identity provider settings, used when the authentication mode accepts an external OAuth2 token.

---Which authentication mode is enforced on the agent's HTTP API.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAuthModeEnum "KAGENT_JWT"|"NONE"|"OAUTH2"

---Toggles for the agent's built-in capabilities, such as network access and web search.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsBuiltinsConfig
---@field network? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the agent can make outbound network requests. Defaults to true.
---@field search? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the agent can perform web searches. Defaults to true.
---@field searchApiKey? string|distilled.Null API key for the configured search provider, when the provider requires one.
---@field searchProvider? string|distilled.Null Which search engine the agent uses for web searches. Defaults to 'duckduckgo'.
---@field toolsDeny? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsBuiltinsConfigToolsDenyList|distilled.Null Tools this agent must not be offered, as glob patterns matched against the tool name ('*' = any run of characters). The 'builtins' flags above are all-or-nothing per subsystem — 'relay' exposes twenty 'relay_*' tools or none. A product built on kadk routinely wants *most* of a subsystem plus a composite of its own, and then finds the model reaching past the composite for the primitives it wraps: offered both 'revision_room' and 'relay_create_room', a model will happily assemble the room by hand and skip everything the composite also did. Naming the primitives here is how the product says 'that path is mine to own'.
---@field wizard? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the agent can reconfigure its own settings, such as its model or memory, from within a conversation. Off by default; only available to an administrator caller when enabled.

---Tools this agent must not be offered, as glob patterns matched against the tool name ('*' = any run of characters). The 'builtins' flags above are all-or-nothing per subsystem — 'relay' exposes twenty 'relay_*' tools or none. A product built on kadk routinely wants *most* of a subsystem plus a composite of its own, and then finds the model reaching past the composite for the primitives it wraps: offered both 'revision_room' and 'relay_create_room', a model will happily assemble the room by hand and skip everything the composite also did. Naming the primitives here is how the product says 'that path is mine to own'.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsBuiltinsConfigToolsDenyList string[]

---Messaging-platform integrations, such as Telegram and Webex, the agent can send and receive messages through.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsChannelsConfig
---@field telegram? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsTelegramChannelConfig|distilled.Null Telegram integration settings. Unset means Telegram is not connected.
---@field webex? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsWebexChannelConfig|distilled.Null Webex integration settings. Unset means Webex is not connected.

---Templated AI agent configuration
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsConfig
---@field agent? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentConfig|distilled.Null The agent's identity settings, such as its display name.
---@field auth? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAuthConfig|distilled.Null Authentication settings for the agent's HTTP API. Unset falls back to requiring a token issued by the agent itself.
---@field builtins? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsBuiltinsConfig|distilled.Null Toggles for the agent's built-in capabilities, such as network access and web search.
---@field channels? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsChannelsConfig|distilled.Null Messaging-platform integrations, such as Telegram and Webex, the agent can send and receive messages through.
---@field exec? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsExecConfig|distilled.Null Remote command-execution settings. Unset or disabled means the agent cannot run shell commands.
---@field llm? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsLlmConfig|distilled.Null The language model this agent uses to respond, including sampling settings and failover targets.
---@field mcpIndexer? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMcpIndexerConfig|distilled.Null Settings for searchable tool indexing, required when any connected tool server uses indexed mode instead of listing all its tools directly.
---@field mcpServers? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsConfigMcpServersMap|distilled.Null Connected MCP tool servers, keyed by a caller-chosen server name.
---@field memory? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMemoryConfig|distilled.Null Long-term memory settings that let the agent retain and later recall facts across conversations.
---@field profiles? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentsConfig|distilled.Null Specialized sub-personas this agent can delegate tasks to.
---@field providers? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsConfigProvidersMap|distilled.Null Shared pool of language-model provider connections, keyed by a caller-chosen provider id and referenced by name elsewhere in this configuration.
---@field relay? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsRelayConfig|distilled.Null Settings for hosting a local messaging relay that other participants can join.
---@field skills? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsSkillsConfig|distilled.Null Reusable skills the agent can invoke: named bundles of instructions it can follow on demand.
---@field soul? string|distilled.Null The agent's persona and system prompt: free-form text describing who it is, how it should behave, and any standing instructions it should always follow.
---@field toolPermissions? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsToolPermissionsConfig|distilled.Null Rules applied to every tool call, matched on its name, arguments and what triggered the turn: before the call runs and — for a rule that says so — on what it returned. A matching rule allows the call, refuses it, asks a human, or defers to an LLM reviewer.
---@field version? string|distilled.Null Configuration format version. Defaults to '1.0' for agents created before this field existed.
---@field workspace? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsWorkspace|distilled.Null The agent's file storage: an ordered list of mount points and the backend serving each one.

