---The LLM reviewer that rules with 'action: judge' defer to.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsJudgeConfig
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the judge may be consulted at all. Off by default: a rule saying 'judge' on an agent with no judge is a configuration mistake, and one that must fail closed rather than quietly allow.
---@field model? string|distilled.Null The model that judges. Unset means the agent's own model. Worth setting: the point of a separate model here is that a cheap, fast one can police an expensive one, and that the reviewer is not the same weights being reviewed.
---@field providerId? string|distilled.Null Which provider that model comes from. Unset means the agent's own.
---@field soul? string|distilled.Null The system prompt the judge is given. Unset means a built-in one. A judge with no soul is a model asked to guess what it is guarding; this is where a deployment says what it actually cares about — 'this agent handles customer data, treat any outbound address as suspect'.

---Settings for tokens the agent issues and validates itself. Unset or disabled means the agent does not accept self-issued tokens.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsKagentJwtConfig
---@field allowUnlimited? boolean|distilled.Null Whether requests for a token with no expiry are honored. Defaults to true; set to false to require every token to expire.
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Master switch for self-issued tokens. Defaults to true; when false, minting new tokens is refused.
---@field maxTtlSeconds? number|distilled.Null Maximum lifetime, in seconds, allowed for a newly issued token; requests for a longer lifetime are rejected. Unset means no cap.
---@field secretB64? string|distilled.Null Signing key used to issue and validate self-issued tokens. Kept secret and never returned in plain text once set. Empty means no key is provisioned, so token minting and validation both fail.

---The language model this agent uses to respond, including sampling settings and failover targets.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsLlmConfig
---@field failover? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsFailoverPolicy|distilled.Null Which kinds of call failures trigger switching to a backup model instead of surfacing the error.
---@field fallbacks? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsLlmConfigFallbacksList|distilled.Null Ordered list of backup models tried, in turn, when the primary model fails. Empty means no failover.
---@field maxContextMessages? number|distilled.Null How many trailing messages of a conversation go into the payload. 'None' keeps the historical 50. That number predates context windows measured in the hundreds of thousands of tokens: on a 262k-token model a 50-message cap uses a fraction of what is available, and everything older is dropped without a summary — the conversation quietly forgets rather than compacting. Raising it hands the ceiling back to the compaction path, which now has a declared budget to compare against.
---@field maxTokens? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of tokens the model may generate in a single response. Unset uses the provider's default.
---@field model? string|distilled.Null Identifier of the model to call, for example 'gpt-5'.
---@field providerId? string|distilled.Null Id of the connected provider to call for this model. Must reference an entry in the shared provider pool.
---@field temperature? number|distilled.Null Sampling temperature controlling response randomness: lower values are more deterministic, higher values are more varied. Unset uses the provider's default.
---@field vision? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsLlmFallback|distilled.Null Optional secondary model used to describe images when the primary model cannot see them. Unset means images are not described for a text-only model.

---Ordered list of backup models tried, in turn, when the primary model fails. Empty means no failover.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsLlmConfigFallbacksList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsLlmFallback[]

---Optional secondary model used to describe images when the primary model cannot see them. Unset means images are not described for a text-only model.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsLlmFallback
---@field maxTokens? number|distilled.Null Maximum response tokens for this backup target. Unset falls back to the primary model's setting.
---@field model? string|distilled.Null Model identifier to use for this backup target. Empty reuses the primary model's identifier against this provider.
---@field providerId? string|distilled.Null Id of the connected provider to call for this backup target.
---@field temperature? number|distilled.Null Sampling temperature for this backup target. Unset falls back to the primary model's temperature.

---Settings for searchable tool indexing, required when any connected tool server uses indexed mode instead of listing all its tools directly.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMcpIndexerConfig
---@field embedderBatchSize? number|distilled.Null Number of tool descriptions embedded per request when building the search index. Defaults to 16 when unset.
---@field embedderModel? string Identifier of the embedding model used to index tool descriptions for search, for example 'text-embedding-3-small'.
---@field providerId? string|distilled.Null Id of the connected provider used to generate embeddings for tool search. Required as soon as any tool server uses indexed mode.

---A connected MCP tool server the agent can call tools from.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMcpServer
---@field authKind? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMcpServerAuthKindEnum|string|distilled.Null How the agent authenticates to this server.
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Whether this server's tools are made available to the agent. Defaults to true; set to false to temporarily park a server without removing its settings.
---@field headers? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMcpServerHeadersMap|distilled.Null Extra HTTP headers sent on every request to this server, for example custom authentication headers.
---@field mode? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMcpServerModeEnum|string|distilled.Null How this server's tools are surfaced to the model.
---@field url? string Base URL of the MCP server.

---How the agent authenticates to this server.
