---Extra HTTP headers sent on every request to this server, for example custom authentication headers.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMcpServerHeadersMap { [string]: string }

---How this server's tools are surfaced to the model.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMcpServerModeEnum "FLAT"|"INDEXED"

---Long-term memory settings that let the agent retain and later recall facts across conversations.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMemoryConfig
---@field consolidateOnTurnEnd? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the agent reviews each conversation turn to capture any durable facts it did not already record. Defaults to true.
---@field consolidationCron? string|distilled.Null Schedule, as a five-field cron expression, for the periodic pass that merges duplicate facts and promotes frequently reinforced ones. Defaults to daily at 3 AM.
---@field consolidationMaxRounds? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of internal steps the end-of-turn memory review may take. Defaults to 3.
---@field corePredicates? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMemoryConfigCorePredicatesList|distilled.Null Fact categories eligible for automatic promotion to permanent status when reinforced. Empty disables automatic promotion; facts can still be promoted manually.
---@field embedderBatchSize? number|distilled.Null Number of facts embedded per request when building the memory index. Defaults to 16.
---@field embedderModel? string|distilled.Null Identifier of the embedding model used to index remembered facts for recall. Required when memory is enabled.
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Master switch for the memory feature. When false, the agent retains no long-term facts.
---@field gcCron? string|distilled.Null Schedule, as a five-field cron expression, for the periodic cleanup pass that evicts low-value facts once storage exceeds its soft limit. Defaults to hourly.
---@field gcMaxSize? number|distilled.Null Hard upper bound on the number of stored facts, used as a safety cap against runaway growth. Defaults to 20000.
---@field gcMinRetention? number|distilled.Null Minimum retention score, from 0 to 1 with no unit, a non-permanent fact must keep to survive cleanup; facts scoring below this are marked for eviction. Defaults to 0.15.
---@field gcSoftLimit? number|distilled.Null Number of stored facts above which cleanup starts evicting low-value ones, stopping once storage is back down to 90% of this value. Defaults to 10000.
---@field halfLifeDays? number|distilled.Null Number of days after which a fact's retention score decays by half. Higher values make facts fade more slowly. Defaults to 45.
---@field identityPromotionThreshold? number|distilled.Null Number of times a fact in a core category must be reinforced before it is promoted to permanent status and never evicted. Defaults to 5.
---@field inferenceLlmFallback? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the model is consulted to classify facts the automatic pass could not resolve on its own. Defaults to true; set to false to keep consolidation fully automatic.
---@field mergeSimilarityThreshold? number|distilled.Null Similarity threshold, from 0 to 1, above which two facts about the same subject are merged during cleanup. Defaults to 0.92.
---@field providerId? string|distilled.Null Id of the connected provider used to generate embeddings for stored facts. Required when memory is enabled.
---@field ruleIdleGcDays? number|distilled.Null Number of days a derived rule may go unused before cleanup removes it. Defaults to 60.
---@field rulesMax? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of derived rules retained. Older or unused rules are cleaned up during consolidation. Defaults to 256.

---Fact categories eligible for automatic promotion to permanent status when reinforced. Empty disables automatic promotion; facts can still be promoted manually.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMemoryConfigCorePredicatesList string[]

---Manual overrides for what a specific model can do, used when the built-in defaults for that model are wrong or unknown for this deployment.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsModelCapabilityOverride
---@field contextWindow? number|distilled.Null Maximum context window, in tokens, that this model accepts. Unset uses the built-in default for the model.
---@field tools? boolean|distilled.Null Whether this model can call tools. Unset uses the built-in default for the model.
---@field vision? boolean|distilled.Null Whether this model can understand images. Unset uses the built-in default for the model.

---Which storage backend serves this mount; determines which of the other fields apply.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMountBackendEnum "BLOB"|"FS"|"S3"|"SQL"

---One workspace mount: a logical path plus the storage backend that serves it (ephemeral filesystem, persistent blob store, SQLite-backed store, or an operator-supplied S3™ compatible bucket).
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMountConfig
---@field accessKey? string|distilled.Null Access key used to authenticate to the bucket.
---@field backend? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsMountBackendEnum|string Which storage backend serves this mount; determines which of the other fields apply.
---@field bucket? string|distilled.Null Name of the bucket this mount reads and writes to.
---@field endpoint? string|distilled.Null Endpoint URL of the S3™-compatible storage service.
---@field maxFileBytes? number|distilled.Null Maximum size, in bytes, allowed for a single file in this mount. Defaults to 8 MiB when unset.
---@field maxFiles? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of files allowed in this mount. Unset means no cap.
---@field maxTotalBytes? number|distilled.Null Maximum total size, in bytes, allowed across all files in this mount. Defaults to 256 MiB when unset.
---@field path? string Absolute path where this mount appears in the agent's filesystem, for example '/' or '/tmp'.
---@field prefix? string|distilled.Null Key prefix within the bucket under which this mount's files are stored. Empty means the bucket root.
---@field region? string|distilled.Null Region of the bucket. Defaults to 'us-east-1'.
---@field ro? boolean|distilled.Null When true, writes and deletes under this mount are rejected.
---@field secretKey? string|distilled.Secret|distilled.Null Secret key used to authenticate to the bucket. Kept secret and never returned in plain text once set.

---External identity provider settings, used when the authentication mode accepts an external OAuth2 token.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsOAuth2Config
---@field audience? string Expected audience value that a presented token must carry to be accepted.
---@field issuer? string Base URL of the external identity provider that issues tokens for this agent.
---@field jwksUri? string|distilled.Null Explicit JWKS endpoint used to verify token signatures. Unset falls back to the identity provider's well-known JWKS location.
---@field ownerSub? string|distilled.Null Stable identifier of the agent's owner at the identity provider. A presented token's subject must match this value to be accepted.
---@field requiredScopes? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsOAuth2ConfigRequiredScopesList|distilled.Null Scopes a presented token must carry to be accepted. Empty means no scope is required.

---Scopes a presented token must carry to be accepted. Empty means no scope is required.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsOAuth2ConfigRequiredScopesList string[]

---One tool-permission rule: which tool calls it matches, and what to do with them.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRule
---@field action? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRuleActionEnum|string What to do with a matching call.
---@field args? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRuleArgsMap|distilled.Null Argument constraints, as 'path-glob -> value-glob', ALL of which must hold for the rule to match. The call's arguments are flattened to 'path -> value' pairs before matching ('{'a':{'b':[1,2]}}' becomes 'a.b.0 -> 1', 'a.b.1 -> 2'), so one entry means 'some argument whose path matches the key has a value matching the pattern'. A '!' prefix on the value inverts it into '… and none of them matches', which is how an allowlist is written: '{'url': '!https://*.ovh.net/*'}' is every URL but ours. '!' flips the value test and not the quantifier: both forms ask whether SOME selected value satisfies the test. So a deny rule reading '{'url': '!https://*.ovh.net/*'}' still fires on a call carrying two URLs of which only one is foreign — which is the point of it. A rule about an argument that is absent entirely never matches, in either form: absence is not a value to have an opinion about, and a rule that fired on it would fire on every unrelated call.
---@field phase? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRulePhaseEnum|string|distilled.Null Whether this rule is evaluated before the call runs or after it returned. Defaults to 'before'.
---@field reason? string|distilled.Null Why this rule exists. Shown to the model in the refusal and written to the log. Worth filling in: it is the only part of this rule the model can act on.
---@field result? string|distilled.Null Value-glob over the text the tool returned. 'phase: after' only. Matched against the raw result, not flattened into paths the way 'args' is: a result is prose far more often than it is a shape, and an author writing a rule about one should not have to know whether this particular tool happened to wrap it in JSON. '*' spans everything, so ''*-----BEGIN * PRIVATE KEY*'' is a substring test, and a leading '!' inverts it exactly as it does in 'args'. A rule with no 'result' matches every result, which is how 'refer everything this tool brings back to the judge' is written.
---@field tool? string|distilled.Null Glob over the tool name. '*' matches any run of characters, including an empty one, so a rule left at its default matches every tool.
---@field triggers? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRuleTriggersList|distilled.Null Trigger kinds this rule applies to ('http', 'invoke', 'messaging', 'cron', 'scheduled', 'subagent'). Empty means every trigger.
---@field unattended? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRuleActionEnum|string|distilled.Null What an 'ask' becomes on a turn with no human to ask. Defaults to 'deny'; ignored unless 'action' is 'ask'.

---What to do with a matching call.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRuleActionEnum "ALLOW"|"ASK"|"DENY"|"JUDGE"

---Argument constraints, as 'path-glob -> value-glob', ALL of which must hold for the rule to match. The call's arguments are flattened to 'path -> value' pairs before matching ('{'a':{'b':[1,2]}}' becomes 'a.b.0 -> 1', 'a.b.1 -> 2'), so one entry means 'some argument whose path matches the key has a value matching the pattern'. A '!' prefix on the value inverts it into '… and none of them matches', which is how an allowlist is written: '{'url': '!https://*.ovh.net/*'}' is every URL but ours. '!' flips the value test and not the quantifier: both forms ask whether SOME selected value satisfies the test. So a deny rule reading '{'url': '!https://*.ovh.net/*'}' still fires on a call carrying two URLs of which only one is foreign — which is the point of it. A rule about an argument that is absent entirely never matches, in either form: absence is not a value to have an opinion about, and a rule that fired on it would fire on every unrelated call.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRuleArgsMap { [string]: string }

---Whether this rule is evaluated before the call runs or after it returned. Defaults to 'before'.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRulePhaseEnum "AFTER"|"BEFORE"

---What started the turn a tool-permission rule applies to
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRuleTriggerEnum "CRON"|"HTTP"|"INVOKE"|"MESSAGING"|"SCHEDULED"|"SUBAGENT"

---Trigger kinds this rule applies to ('http', 'invoke', 'messaging', 'cron', 'scheduled', 'subagent'). Empty means every trigger.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRuleTriggersList (ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsPermissionRuleTriggerEnum|string)[]

---A language-model provider connection, referenced by id from other configuration blocks that need to call a model.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsProviderConfig
---@field aiEndpoints? boolean|distilled.Null Materialize this provider from the OVHcloud AI Endpoints preset. Only accepted on the reserved provider id, which no other provider may use, and on a single provider. Mutually exclusive with apiBase and displayName, which the preset supplies. Defaults to false. Refused when the deployment has the preset disabled.
---@field aiEndpointsIntegratedAuth? boolean|distilled.Null Have OVHcloud mint this provider's bearer token itself. Requires aiEndpoints, and is mutually exclusive with apiKey. Defaults to false. Refused when the deployment has the preset's integrated authentication disabled.
---@field apiBase? string|distilled.Null Base URL of the provider's API endpoint, for example 'https://api.openai.com/v1'. No trailing slash.
---@field apiKey? string|distilled.Secret|distilled.Null API key used to authenticate to this provider. Kept secret and never returned in plain text once set.
---@field displayName? string|distilled.Null Human-readable label for this provider, shown in the interface. Defaults to the provider's id when empty.
---@field models? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsProviderConfigModelsMap|distilled.Null Per-model capability overrides for models hosted by this provider, keyed by model id.

---Per-model capability overrides for models hosted by this provider, keyed by model id.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsProviderConfigModelsMap { [string]: ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsModelCapabilityOverride }

---Settings for hosting a local messaging relay that other participants can join.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsRelayConfig
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Master switch for hosting a relay. When false, the relay and its rooms are not available.
---@field maxMessagesPerRoom? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of messages retained per room. Unset means unlimited.
---@field maxRooms? number|distilled.Null Maximum number of rooms this relay may host. Unset means unlimited.
---@field roomCreation? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsRelayRoomCreationEnum|string|distilled.Null Controls who may create a new room on this relay: by default only the host can create rooms, but this can be relaxed so that any authenticated member creates one simply by joining a room that does not yet exist.

---Who may create a new room on a relay
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsRelayRoomCreationEnum "OPEN"|"OWNER"

---Temporary per-conversation working files the agent can generate, download into, and re-read across turns, cleaned up automatically after a retention period. Unset means on with defaults.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsScratchpadConfig
---@field cleanupCron? string|distilled.Null Schedule, as a five-field cron expression, for the pass that deletes expired scratchpads. Defaults to daily at 4:30 AM.
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Whether scratchpads are available. Unset means automatically on whenever the agent has durable file storage; set to false to disable them explicitly.
---@field maxDownloadBytes? number|distilled.Null Largest single download, in bytes, that may be saved to a scratchpad. Defaults to 25 MiB.
---@field path? string|distilled.Null Absolute path of the directory holding one subdirectory per conversation. Defaults to '/scratchpad'.
---@field retentionDays? number|distilled.Null Number of days a conversation's scratchpad may go untouched before it is deleted. Defaults to 7.
---@field spillBytes? number|distilled.Null Size, in bytes, above which a fetched page is saved to the scratchpad and summarized instead of being returned in full. Defaults to 128 KiB.

---A single skill definition: what it does and how the agent should perform it.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsSkillSeed
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Short summary of what this skill does, shown to the user when listing available skills.
---@field instructions? string|distilled.Null Detailed instructions the agent follows when invoking this skill.

---Reusable skills the agent can invoke: named bundles of instructions it can follow on demand.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsSkillsConfig
---@field builtins? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsSkillsConfigBuiltinsList|distilled.Null Ids of built-in skills to enable, or '-id' to disable one that is on by default.
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the agent's skills are offered to the model. Absent means yes. When false the prompt catalogue and the 'skill_*' tools go away, so the model is not told about them and cannot invoke them — but their files stay mounted in the workspace ('workspace.skills_path', default '/skills'), where a model with filesystem tools can still read them.
---@field items? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsSkillsConfigItemsMap|distilled.Null Skills defined directly in this configuration, keyed by skill name. Skills created through other means are left untouched.

---Ids of built-in skills to enable, or '-id' to disable one that is on by default.
