---Target specification for updating a block storage volume. This body is the complete desired specification: every field below is replaced by what the request carries, and a field left out is cleared rather than carried over from the stored specification, so read the volume first and restate every value you want to keep. The create-only fields location, encryption and createFrom cannot be changed once the volume exists; they are deliberately absent from this model and sending one is rejected as an unknown field.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudBlockStorageBlockUpdateTargetSpec
---@field name string Desired volume name
---@field size number Size of the volume in GB. The size can only be increased (extend); shrinking a volume is not supported. Leaving it out, or sending 0, is rejected with a 400
---@field volumeType? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudBlockStorageVolumeTypeEnum|string|distilled.Null Target volume type. Changing this triggers an online retype (migration).

