---Instance group (placement group)
---
---A Public Cloud instance group, backed by an OpenStack/Nova server group, that constrains how its member instances are placed relative to one another (see policy and PolicyEnum: AFFINITY / ANTI_AFFINITY).
---
---An instance group is immutable once created: there is no update (PUT) route, and its membership is fixed. Instances join a group only at instance-creation time, through the instance's targetSpec.group field — they cannot be added to or removed from a group afterward. The only lifecycle operations are create (POST), read (GET/LIST) and delete (DELETE).
---
---The object follows the standard envelope: targetSpec is the desired specification supplied on creation, while currentState reflects what the backend actually reports (including the current members).
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroup
---@field checksum? string Checksum Computed hash of the current target specification, used for optimistic concurrency control. Because an instance group has no update route, this value never changes after creation.
---@field createdAt? string Creation date Timestamp at which the instance group was created, in RFC 3339 format.
---@field currentState? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroupCurrentState|distilled.Null Current state Actual state of the instance group as reported by the backend (OpenStack/Nova server group), including its current members. This is read-only and reflects reality, in contrast to targetSpec which is the desired specification supplied on creation. May be null while the group is still being provisioned and no backend state is known yet.
---@field currentTasks? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroupCurrentTasksList|distilled.Null Current tasks Asynchronous operations currently running against this instance group (for example the initial provisioning or the deletion). Empty or null when no operation is in progress.
---@field id? string Identifier Unique identifier of the instance group, assigned at creation and used to reference it on the GET/DELETE routes.
---@field resourceStatus? ovh.cloud_v2.CommonResourceStatusEnum Resource status Lifecycle status of the instance group in the system (for example whether it is being created, ready, or being deleted). Reflects readiness of the resource, not the placement policy itself.
---@field targetSpec? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroupTargetSpec Target specification Desired specification of the instance group as supplied on creation (name, location and placement policy). Since an instance group cannot be updated, this specification is fixed for the lifetime of the group; compare it against currentState to see what the backend actually provisioned.

---Current instance group state
---
---Actual state of an instance group as reported by the backend (OpenStack/Nova server group). This is read-only: it reflects what the backend observes, in contrast to the desired InstanceGroupTargetSpec supplied on creation.
---
---Besides the group's name, location and placement policy, it exposes the current membership. Membership is fixed once instances are created: instances join a group only at instance-creation time via the instance's targetSpec.group field, and there is no route to add or remove members afterward.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroupCurrentState
---@field location? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudCommonLocation Location Region (and, where applicable, availability zone) where the instance group and its member instances are deployed, as observed on the backend.
---@field members? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroupCurrentStateMembersList|distilled.Null Members Instances currently belonging to this group, each referenced by its identifier (see InstanceGroupMemberRef). Membership is determined at instance-creation time via the instance's targetSpec.group field and cannot be changed afterward. Null or empty when the group has no member instances.
---@field name? string Name Display name of the instance group as reported by the backend. Fixed for the lifetime of the group, since instance groups cannot be updated.
---@field policy? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupPolicyEnum Placement policy Placement policy currently enforced for the group's members (see PolicyEnum): AFFINITY packs members onto the same hypervisor, ANTI_AFFINITY spreads them across distinct hypervisors. Mirrors the underlying OpenStack/Nova server group policy and is fixed at creation.

---Members
---
---Instances currently belonging to this group, each referenced by its identifier (see InstanceGroupMemberRef). Membership is determined at instance-creation time via the instance's targetSpec.group field and cannot be changed afterward. Null or empty when the group has no member instances.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroupCurrentStateMembersList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroupMemberRef[]

---Current tasks
---
---Asynchronous operations currently running against this instance group (for example the initial provisioning or the deletion). Empty or null when no operation is in progress.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroupCurrentTasksList ovh.cloud_v2.CommonCurrentTask[]

---Instance group member reference
---
---Reference to a single instance that is a member of an instance group. It appears in the group's currentState.members list and identifies the member by its instance id.
---
---Membership is established at instance-creation time via the instance's targetSpec.group field and is immutable: an instance cannot be added to or removed from a group afterward.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroupMemberRef
---@field id? string Instance identifier Unique identifier of the instance that belongs to the group. Use it to look up the full instance on the compute instance route.

---Desired instance group specification (creation)
---
---User-controlled specification of an instance group, as supplied on creation (POST). It carries every settable field: name, location and placement policy.
---
---All of these fields are immutable once the group exists — an instance group has no update (PUT) route, so this specification is fixed for the lifetime of the group. Membership is not part of this spec: instances join the group only at instance-creation time via the instance's targetSpec.group field.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroupTargetSpec
---@field location ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudCommonLocation Target location Region (and optional availability zone) where the instance group, and therefore its member instances, are placed. Immutable after creation — a group cannot be moved to another region/zone, and its members must be created in this same location.
---@field name string Name Desired display name of the instance group. Immutable after creation, as instance groups cannot be updated.
---@field policy ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupPolicyEnum|string Placement policy Placement policy applied to the group's member instances (see PolicyEnum): AFFINITY packs members onto the same hypervisor, while ANTI_AFFINITY spreads members across distinct hypervisors. This maps to the underlying OpenStack/Nova server group policy and is immutable after creation.

---Instance group placement policy
---
---Scheduling policy that governs how the members of an instance group are placed relative to one another on the underlying hypervisors.
---
---Values
---AFFINITY — Group members are placed onto the same hypervisor host, keeping them physically close together.
---ANTI_AFFINITY — Group members are forced onto different hypervisor hosts, spreading them apart for higher availability.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupPolicyEnum "AFFINITY"|"ANTI_AFFINITY"

---Image operating system type
---
---Operating system family of an instance image, as tagged on the image in OpenStack Glance. It decides which flavors can boot the image, and Windows images carry a license.
---
---Values
---LINUX — A Linux (or other non-Windows) image for virtual instances.
---WINDOWS — A Microsoft Windows image; it can only boot on Windows flavors.
---BAREMETAL_LINUX — A Linux image for bare-metal instances.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceImageOSTypeEnum "BAREMETAL_LINUX"|"LINUX"|"WINDOWS"

---OpenStack image status
---
---Lifecycle status of an instance image as reported by OpenStack Glance. It describes where the image is in its upload and availability lifecycle.
---
---Values
---QUEUED — The image identifier has been reserved in the image registry, but no image data has been uploaded yet.
---SAVING — The raw image data is currently being uploaded to the image store.
---IMPORTING — The uploaded image data is being imported and processed through the Glance import workflow.
---ACTIVE — The image is fully available and can be used to boot instances.
---DEACTIVATED — Access to the image has been disabled by an administrator; the data is preserved but the image cannot be used to launch instances until reactivated.
---KILLED — An error occurred during upload or import and the image data is not usable.
---PENDING_DELETE — The image has been marked for deletion but its data has not been removed yet; it may still be restorable during the retention delay.
---DELETED — The image has been deleted and its data is scheduled for removal.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceImageStatusEnum "ACTIVE"|"DEACTIVATED"|"DELETED"|"IMPORTING"|"KILLED"|"PENDING_DELETE"|"QUEUED"|"SAVING"

---Image visibility
---
---Controls which projects can see and use an instance image, as defined by OpenStack Glance.
---
---Values
---PUBLIC — The image is visible to and usable by every project.
---PRIVATE — The image is visible only to the project that owns it.
---SHARED — The image is visible only to the owning project and the specific projects it has been explicitly shared with (image members).
---COMMUNITY — The image is usable by every project but is hidden from default image listings, so it must be requested explicitly.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceImageVisibilityEnum "COMMUNITY"|"PRIVATE"|"PUBLIC"|"SHARED"

---Compute instance
---
---A Public Cloud compute instance: a virtual machine provisioned from a flavor and an image, connected to one or more networks and backed by block volumes.
---
---The resource follows the standard desired-state / observed-state model:
---targetSpec holds the specification you asked for.
---currentState reflects what the compute backend actually reports.
---resourceStatus and currentTasks describe the reconciliation between the two.
---
---Updates are performed by sending a new targetSpec on the PUT route; the requested operations (rename, resize, power change, volume attach/detach, share attach/detach) are derived from the diff.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstance
---@field checksum? string Concurrency-control checksum Computed hash representing the current targetSpec value. It enables optional optimistic concurrency control: the value returned by a GET may be sent back in the PUT and action payloads, and the request is then rejected with a 409 checksum-mismatch conflict if it no longer matches server-side (because another request modified the instance in the meantime). Sending no checksum skips that check and forces the write (last-write-wins).
---@field createdAt? string Creation date of the instance, as an ISO 8601 / RFC 3339 timestamp.
---@field currentState? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentState|distilled.Null Observed state Current observed state of the instance as reported by the compute backend (name, flavor, image, location, power state, networks, attached volumes, attached shares, security groups). It is null while the instance is still being created and no backend state is available yet.
---@field currentTasks? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentTasksList|distilled.Null In-progress operations Ongoing asynchronous tasks reconciling currentState toward targetSpec (for example a create, resize, reboot, volume attach or share attach). Poll the instance until this list is empty and resourceStatus is READY to know the requested change has been applied.
---@field id? string Unique identifier of the instance.
---@field resourceStatus? ovh.cloud_v2.CommonResourceStatusEnum Resource lifecycle status High-level readiness of the instance in the system (for example CREATING, READY, UPDATING, DELETING, ERROR). This is distinct from currentState.powerState, which carries the lower-level OpenStack administrative power state of the virtual machine.
---@field targetSpec? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceReadTargetSpec Desired specification Last target specification requested for the instance. On update, the difference between the previous and the new targetSpec determines the operations performed (rename, resize, power change, and declarative volume/share attach-detach).
---@field updatedAt? string Last modification date of the instance, as an ISO 8601 / RFC 3339 timestamp.

---Instance action parameters
---
---Optional parameters refining an imperative instance action. Each field applies only to a specific action type (see InstanceActionTypeEnum) and is ignored for other actions.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceActionParameters
---@field hard? boolean|distilled.Null Hard reboot Applies only to the REBOOT action. When true, performs a hard reboot (power cycle) instead of a graceful, soft reboot. Defaults to a soft reboot when omitted.
---@field imageId? string|distilled.Null Rescue image Applies only to the RESCUE action. Identifier of the image to boot the instance from while in rescue mode. When omitted, the backend selects a default rescue image.

---Instance action type
---
---Imperative action that can be triggered on an instance to change its administrative or operational state.
---
---Values
---LOCK — Lock the instance to prevent further actions on it, protecting it from accidental or unauthorized operations.
---UNLOCK — Remove a previously set lock, re-enabling actions on the instance.
---REBOOT — Restart the instance.
---RESCUE — Boot the instance into rescue mode from a rescue image so its root disk can be inspected or repaired.
---UNRESCUE — Return the instance from rescue mode to normal operation.
---STOP — Power off the instance; its resources remain allocated.
---START — Power on a stopped instance.
---SHELVE — Power off the instance and release its compute resources so it can be resumed later.
---UNSHELVE — Resume a shelved instance.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceActionTypeEnum "LOCK"|"REBOOT"|"RESCUE"|"SHELVE"|"START"|"STOP"|"UNLOCK"|"UNRESCUE"|"UNSHELVE"

---Instance action availability
---
---One instance action type and whether it can currently be triggered on the instance through the action endpoint.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceAvailableAction
---@field available? boolean Whether the action can currently be triggered through the action endpoint. A call with an unavailable action is refused.
---@field name? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceActionTypeEnum Action type, as accepted by the action endpoint

---Observed instance state
---
---Current observed state of the instance as reported by the compute backend (OpenStack/Nova). It is read-only and reflects what actually exists, as opposed to targetSpec which holds what was requested.
---
---Some collections (notably shares) are only populated on a GET of a single instance and are omitted from the LIST response.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentState
---@field availableActions? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentStateAvailableActionsList Available actions Availability of every instance action type given the current state of the instance. Always contains exactly one entry per InstanceActionTypeEnum value, in the order of that enum, each flagged with whether it can currently be triggered through the action endpoint. For example, when the instance is locked only UNLOCK is available; while a task is in progress on the instance or when it is in error, none is available.
---@field flavor? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceFlavor Flavor Observed flavor of the instance with full details (name, vCPUs, RAM, local disk). See InstanceFlavor.
---@field group? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceGroupRef|distilled.Null Placement group Reference to the instance (placement) group the instance belongs to, or null when it is not part of any group. Set at creation and immutable thereafter.
---@field hostId? string|distilled.Null Opaque identifier of the physical host the instance is running on, as exposed by OpenStack. Null when not available.
---@field image? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceImage|distilled.Null Image Observed image the instance was booted from, with full details (name, size, status). Null for boot-from-volume instances, which have no image. See InstanceImage.
---@field location? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceLocation Location Observed region and availability zone where the instance is provisioned. See InstanceLocation.
---@field locked? boolean Lock state Whether the instance is locked against modifications. When locked, mutating actions are refused until it is unlocked (see the LOCK/UNLOCK actions in InstanceActionTypeEnum).
---@field name? string Observed display name of the instance.
---@field networks? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentStateNetworksList|distilled.Null Networks Observed network interfaces of the instance, with full details (network, subnet, gateway and per-interface addresses). One entry per network, plus at most one entry without an id for the public (Ext-Net) interface. Every address of the instance is reported through the entry's addresses list, each address typed FIXED, FLOATING or ADDITIONAL — there is no separate scalar address field. See InstanceNetwork.
---@field powerState? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstancePowerStateEnum Power state Actual administrative power state of the instance as reported by OpenStack (see PowerStateEnum). This may transiently differ from targetSpec.powerState while a power transition is in progress.
---@field projectId? string Identifier of the Public Cloud project the instance belongs to.
---@field securityGroups? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentStateSecurityGroupsList|distilled.Null Security groups References to the security groups currently attached to the instance's ports.
---@field shares? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentStateSharesList|distilled.Null Shares Observed instance-side share attachments. Only populated on a GET of a single instance (never in list responses). Mixing per-share access rules (managed directly on the share resource) with instance-side attach on the same share is unsupported and will show the share OUT_OF_SYNC. See InstanceShare.
---@field sshKeyName? string|distilled.Null Name of the SSH key pair injected into the instance at boot, or null when none was provided.
---@field userId? string Identifier of the OpenStack user that owns the instance.
---@field volumes? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentStateVolumesList|distilled.Null Volumes Observed block volumes attached to the instance, with details (name, size). See InstanceVolume.

---Available actions
---
---Availability of every instance action type given the current state of the instance. Always contains exactly one entry per InstanceActionTypeEnum value, in the order of that enum, each flagged with whether it can currently be triggered through the action endpoint. For example, when the instance is locked only UNLOCK is available; while a task is in progress on the instance or when it is in error, none is available.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentStateAvailableActionsList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceAvailableAction[]

---Networks
---
---Observed network interfaces of the instance, with full details (network, subnet, gateway and per-interface addresses). One entry per network, plus at most one entry without an id for the public (Ext-Net) interface. Every address of the instance is reported through the entry's addresses list, each address typed FIXED, FLOATING or ADDITIONAL — there is no separate scalar address field. See InstanceNetwork.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentStateNetworksList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetwork[]

---Security groups
---
---References to the security groups currently attached to the instance's ports.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentStateSecurityGroupsList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudSecurityGroupSecurityGroupRef[]

---Shares
---
---Observed instance-side share attachments. Only populated on a GET of a single instance (never in list responses).
---
---Mixing per-share access rules (managed directly on the share resource) with instance-side attach on the same share is unsupported and will show the share OUT_OF_SYNC. See InstanceShare.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentStateSharesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceShare[]

---Volumes
---
---Observed block volumes attached to the instance, with details (name, size). See InstanceVolume.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentStateVolumesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceVolume[]

---In-progress operations
---
---Ongoing asynchronous tasks reconciling currentState toward targetSpec (for example a create, resize, reboot, volume attach or share attach). Poll the instance until this list is empty and resourceStatus is READY to know the requested change has been applied.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceCurrentTasksList ovh.cloud_v2.CommonCurrentTask[]

---Instance flavor details
---
---Observed flavor of an instance, carrying the full sizing details as reported by the backend. Used in currentState; the creation/update side references a flavor by id through InstanceFlavorRef.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceFlavor
---@field bandwidth? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceFlavorBandwidth|distilled.Null Network bandwidth of the flavor, in Mbit/s. Null when the flavor is not in the catalog.
---@field disk? number Size of the flavor's local root disk, in GB.
---@field gpus? number Number of physical GPUs provided by the flavor, 0 for flavors without GPU.
---@field id? string Unique identifier of the flavor.
---@field name? string Human-readable flavor name (for example the commercial flavor label).
---@field ram? number Amount of RAM provided by the flavor, in MB.
---@field vcpus? number Number of virtual CPUs provided by the flavor.

---Instance flavor reference
---
---User-controlled reference to the flavor that sizes the instance, used in targetSpec. It carries only the flavor id; the full observed sizing is exposed in currentState through InstanceFlavor.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceFlavorRef
---@field id string Identifier of the flavor to size the instance with. Changing it on update triggers a resize.

---Instance group reference
---
---Reference to the instance (placement) group the instance belongs to, controlling affinity/anti-affinity placement. Used in targetSpec to place the instance at creation and echoed in currentState.
---
---The group is set only at creation time and is immutable afterward — OpenStack/Nova server groups cannot be changed, so membership cannot be modified on a running instance.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceGroupRef
---@field id string Identifier of the instance group. Honored only at creation time; the group cannot be changed afterward.

---Instance image details
---
---Observed image an instance was booted from, carrying the full details as reported by OpenStack Glance. Used in currentState; the creation/update side references an image by id through InstanceImageRef.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceImage
---@field defaultUser? string|distilled.Null Default login user of the image, as set by its publisher, for example almalinux or ubuntu. Null when the image declares none.
---@field deprecated? boolean Whether the image is flagged as deprecated. A deprecated image can still boot existing instances but is no longer recommended for new ones.
---@field id? string Unique identifier of the image.
---@field name? string|distilled.Null Human-readable image name, or null when not reported by the backend.
---@field size? number|distilled.Null Size of the image, in bytes. Null when the backend does not report it.
---@field status? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceImageStatusEnum|distilled.Null Lifecycle status of the image as reported by Glance (see ImageStatusEnum). Null when not reported.

---Instance image reference
---
---User-controlled reference to the image the instance boots from, used in targetSpec. It carries only the image id; the full observed image is exposed in currentState through InstanceImage.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceImageRef
---@field id string Identifier of the image to boot from. Changing it on update triggers a rebuild of the instance.

---Instance location
---
---Geographic placement of an instance: the region and, optionally, the availability zone within that region. In targetSpec it is the desired placement (immutable after creation); in currentState it is the observed placement.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceLocation
---@field availabilityZone? string|distilled.Null Availability zone Availability zone within the region where the instance is placed. Optional: when omitted at creation the backend selects a zone automatically. Immutable after creation.
---@field region string Region Code of the region where the instance is provisioned (for example GRA11, BHS5). Immutable after creation — an instance cannot be moved to another region.

---Instance network interface (observed)
---
---Observed network interface attached to an instance, with full details as reported by the backend. Used in currentState; the creation/update side declares interfaces through InstanceNetworkRef.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetwork
---@field addresses? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetworkAddressesList|distilled.Null Addresses Every IP address through which the instance is reachable on this interface, each with its type, IP version and MAC address. It carries the interface's fixed addresses and, where applicable, the floating IP associated with it and any additional IPs routed to it. This is the single source of truth for the instance's observed addresses. Null or empty only while no address has been assigned yet. See InstanceNetworkAddress.
---@field gatewayId? string|distilled.Null Identifier of the gateway providing egress for this interface, or null when none applies.
---@field id? string|distilled.Null Identifier of the network this interface is attached to, or null for the public (Ext-Net) interface. There is at most one entry without an id: additional IPs are reported as ADDITIONAL addresses of that public entry instead of forming their own entry.
---@field subnetId? string|distilled.Null Identifier of the subnet this interface draws its fixed address from, or null for an entry without a network id.

---Instance network address
---
---A single IP address bound to an instance network interface, with its associated MAC address, IP version and address type.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetworkAddress
---@field ip? string IP address assigned to the interface (IPv4 or IPv6).
---@field mac? string|distilled.Null MAC address of the interface this IP is bound to. Null when the backend reports no interface for the address, which happens for an additional IP routed to an instance whose public interface has no visible Ext-Net address yet.
---@field type? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetworkAddressTypeEnum Address type How this address reaches the instance: FIXED for an address assigned to the interface itself, FLOATING for a floating IP NAT'd onto it, ADDITIONAL for an additional IP routed to the public interface. See InstanceNetworkAddressTypeEnum.
---@field version? number IP version of the address (4 for IPv4, 6 for IPv6).

---Instance network address type
---
---Nature of an IP address observed on an instance network interface, telling how the address reaches the instance.
---
---Values
---FIXED — An address assigned to the interface itself: the fixed address of a private interface (whether assigned by IPAM or pinned), or the platform-assigned or pinned Ext-Net address of the public interface.
---FLOATING — A floating IP NAT'd onto this interface: the address is not configured on the interface, the network translates it to the interface's fixed address.
---ADDITIONAL — An additional IP (also known as a failover IP, implemented as an ipalias) routed to the instance's public interface.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetworkAddressTypeEnum "ADDITIONAL"|"FIXED"|"FLOATING"

---Addresses
---
---Every IP address through which the instance is reachable on this interface, each with its type, IP version and MAC address. It carries the interface's fixed addresses and, where applicable, the floating IP associated with it and any additional IPs routed to it. This is the single source of truth for the instance's observed addresses. Null or empty only while no address has been assigned yet. See InstanceNetworkAddress.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetworkAddressesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetworkAddress[]

---Instance network reference (desired)
---
---User-controlled entry declaring one network interface to attach to the instance in targetSpec. Which fields are set determines the meaning of the entry:
---* autoAssignPublicIp alone — a public (Ext-Net) interface with a platform-assigned public IP. At most one entry of the list may set it.
---* ip alone, without an id and without a subnetId — a public IP the project already owns: either an additional IP, or an Ext-Net IP of the project in the instance's region. Any other address is rejected. Such an entry implicitly attaches the public (Ext-Net) interface. Several of them are allowed, and they may coexist with an autoAssignPublicIp entry.
---* subnetId, with an optional id — a private interface whose fixed address is assigned by IPAM.
---* subnetId and ip, with an optional id — a private interface where ip pins the fixed address when it falls inside the subnet CIDR, and otherwise designates an EXISTING floating IP to associate with that interface.
---
---When id is omitted on a private interface, the network of subnetId is used. When id is given, subnetId must belong to it.
---
---The enclosing networks list is declarative: adding or removing an entry attaches or detaches the corresponding interface on update.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetworkRef
---@field autoAssignPublicIp? boolean|distilled.Null Auto-assign public IP Whether to attach a public (Ext-Net) interface with a public IP assigned by the platform. Only allowed on an entry that has no id, no subnetId and no ip, and at most one entry of the networks list may set it. Requires the optional instance/usePublicIP IAM action.
---@field id? string|distilled.Null Network Identifier of the private network to attach to. Optional on a private interface: when omitted, the network of subnetId is used. Omit it on an entry declaring public connectivity through autoAssignPublicIp or ip.
---@field ip? string|distilled.Null IP address Address of this interface, whose meaning depends on the sibling fields. Without an id and a subnetId: a public IP the project already owns — an additional IP, or an Ext-Net IP of the project in the instance's region; any other address is rejected, and the entry implicitly attaches the public (Ext-Net) interface. On a private entry (subnetId, with an optional id): pins the interface's fixed address when the address falls inside the subnet CIDR, and otherwise designates an EXISTING floating IP to associate with that interface. A public address requires the optional instance/usePublicIP IAM action.
---@field subnetId? string|distilled.Null Subnet Identifier of the subnet the interface draws its fixed address from. Required for a private interface; leave unset on an entry declaring public connectivity.

---Desired instance specification as returned on read
---
---Last target specification requested for the instance, as returned on read (GET/LIST). It mirrors InstanceTargetSpec but relaxes the create-only constraints: fields that are mandatory at creation are not required here, and image is nullable because boot-from-volume instances have no image.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceReadTargetSpec
---@field flavor? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceFlavorRef Flavor Reference to the flavor that sizes the instance (vCPUs, RAM, local disk). Carries only the flavor id. Mutable: changing the referenced flavor on PUT triggers a resize of the instance.
---@field group? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceGroupRef|distilled.Null Placement group Optional reference to the instance (placement) group the instance is created into, controlling affinity/anti-affinity placement. Immutable: the group is set only at creation time. OpenStack/Nova server groups are immutable — there is no group change on PUT and membership cannot be changed after the instance exists.
---@field image? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceImageRef|distilled.Null Image Reference to the image the instance boots from. Carries only the image id. Mutable: changing the referenced image on PUT triggers a rebuild of the instance from the new image. Null for boot-from-volume instances, which have no backing image.
---@field location? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceLocation Target location Region (and optional availability zone) where the instance is provisioned. Immutable after creation — an instance cannot be moved to another region/zone, which is why location is absent from InstanceUpdateTargetSpec.
---@field name? string Name Desired display name of the instance. Mutable: changing it on PUT triggers a rename.
---@field networks? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceReadTargetSpecNetworksList|distilled.Null Networks Declarative list of network interfaces the instance is attached to. An entry with a subnetId, and an optional id, is a private interface, optionally carrying an ip to pin its fixed address or to associate an existing floating IP; an entry with autoAssignPublicIp alone requests a public (Ext-Net) interface with a platform-assigned public IP; an entry with ip alone attaches a public IP the project already owns, either an additional IP or an Ext-Net IP of the project in the instance's region. See InstanceNetworkRef. The list drives the desired network topology: adding or removing an entry attaches or detaches the corresponding interface on update.
---@field powerState? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstancePowerStateEnum|distilled.Null Power state Desired administrative power state of the instance (see PowerStateEnum: ACTIVE, RESCUE, SHELVED, SHUTOFF). Defaults to ACTIVE when omitted. Mutable: changing it on PUT drives the corresponding power transition (start, stop, shelve, rescue).
---@field securityGroups? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceReadTargetSpecSecurityGroupsList|distilled.Null Security groups Optional list of references to the security groups applied to all of the instance's ports. Each entry carries the security group id. Mutable: changing this list on PUT re-applies the resulting set of security groups to every instance port.
---@field shares? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceReadTargetSpecSharesList|distilled.Null Shares Declarative list of file storage (shares) attached to the instance, managed exactly like volumes: the diff of this list on PUT drives attach/detach. Attaching a share creates a Manila IP access rule for the instance's interface on the share's network — the instance MUST have an interface on that network or the operation errors. Detaching (removing an entry from this list) deletes the matching access rule and is idempotent. Each entry's accessLevel defaults to READ_WRITE when omitted (see InstanceShareRef).
---@field sshKeyName? string|distilled.Null SSH key name Name of the SSH key pair injected into the instance at boot for initial access. Immutable / create-only: the key is injected once during provisioning and cannot be changed afterward, which is why sshKeyName is absent from InstanceUpdateTargetSpec.
---@field volumes? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceReadTargetSpecVolumesList|distilled.Null Volumes Declarative list of block volumes attached to the instance, each referencing a volume by id (see InstanceVolumeRef). Attach/detach is driven by diffing this list on PUT — there is no imperative attach/detach sub-route. Adding a volume reference attaches that volume; removing one detaches it.

---Networks
---
---Declarative list of network interfaces the instance is attached to. An entry with a subnetId, and an optional id, is a private interface, optionally carrying an ip to pin its fixed address or to associate an existing floating IP; an entry with autoAssignPublicIp alone requests a public (Ext-Net) interface with a platform-assigned public IP; an entry with ip alone attaches a public IP the project already owns, either an additional IP or an Ext-Net IP of the project in the instance's region. See InstanceNetworkRef.
---
---The list drives the desired network topology: adding or removing an entry attaches or detaches the corresponding interface on update.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceReadTargetSpecNetworksList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetworkRef[]

---Security groups
---
---Optional list of references to the security groups applied to all of the instance's ports. Each entry carries the security group id.
---
---Mutable: changing this list on PUT re-applies the resulting set of security groups to every instance port.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceReadTargetSpecSecurityGroupsList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudSecurityGroupSecurityGroupRef[]

---Shares
---
---Declarative list of file storage (shares) attached to the instance, managed exactly like volumes: the diff of this list on PUT drives attach/detach.
---
---Attaching a share creates a Manila IP access rule for the instance's interface on the share's network — the instance MUST have an interface on that network or the operation errors. Detaching (removing an entry from this list) deletes the matching access rule and is idempotent. Each entry's accessLevel defaults to READ_WRITE when omitted (see InstanceShareRef).
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceReadTargetSpecSharesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceShareRef[]

---Volumes
---
---Declarative list of block volumes attached to the instance, each referencing a volume by id (see InstanceVolumeRef).
---
---Attach/detach is driven by diffing this list on PUT — there is no imperative attach/detach sub-route. Adding a volume reference attaches that volume; removing one detaches it.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceReadTargetSpecVolumesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceVolumeRef[]

---Instance share attachment (observed)
---
---Observed instance-side share attachment, describing the Manila IP access rule that grants the instance access to a file storage (share).
---
---IMPORTANT: this list is only populated on a GET of a single instance — it is never returned in the LIST response. Mixing per-share access rules managed directly on the share resource with instance-side attach on the SAME share is unsupported and will make the share report OUT_OF_SYNC.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceShare
---@field accessLevel? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudStorageFileFileStorageAccessLevelEnum Access level Observed access level of the access rule for this instance (see FileStorageAccessLevelEnum: READ_ONLY, READ_WRITE).
---@field accessTo? string Access target The instance IP address the Manila access rule targets — the instance's fixed IPv4 address on the share's network.
---@field id? string Share Identifier of the attached file storage (share).
---@field state? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudStorageFileFileStorageAccessRuleStateEnum|distilled.Null Access rule state Observed state of the underlying access rule (see FileStorageAccessRuleStateEnum: ACTIVE, APPLYING, DENYING, ERROR). Null while no state has been reported yet.

---Share attachment reference (desired)
---
---User-controlled reference declaring a file storage (share) to attach to the instance, used within the declarative shares list of targetSpec. It carries the share id and the desired access level for the attachment.
---
---Attaching creates a Manila IP access rule for the instance's interface on the share's network; the enclosing shares list is diffed on update to drive attach/detach, exactly like volumes.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceShareRef
---@field accessLevel? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudStorageFileFileStorageAccessLevelEnum|string|distilled.Null Access level Desired access level granted to the instance for this share (see FileStorageAccessLevelEnum: READ_ONLY, READ_WRITE). Optional: defaults to READ_WRITE when omitted.
---@field id string Share Identifier of the file storage (share) to attach. Adding this reference attaches the share to the instance; removing it from the shares list detaches it.

---Desired instance specification (creation)
---
---User-controlled specification of a compute instance, as supplied on creation (POST). It carries every settable field, including fields that become immutable once the instance exists (location, sshKeyName, group).
---
---Networks, volumes and shares are declarative lists: on update, the requested topology is reconciled by diffing these lists against the current attachments. The PUT route uses a reduced InstanceUpdateTargetSpec that only exposes the mutable fields.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceTargetSpec
---@field flavor ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceFlavorRef Flavor Reference to the flavor that sizes the instance (vCPUs, RAM, local disk). Carries only the flavor id. Mutable: changing the referenced flavor on PUT triggers a resize of the instance.
---@field group? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceGroupRef|distilled.Null Placement group Optional reference to the instance (placement) group the instance is created into, controlling affinity/anti-affinity placement. Immutable: the group is set only at creation time. OpenStack/Nova server groups are immutable — there is no group change on PUT and membership cannot be changed after the instance exists.
---@field image? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceImageRef|distilled.Null Image Reference to the image the instance boots from. Carries only the image id. Mutable: changing the referenced image on PUT triggers a rebuild of the instance from the new image.
---@field location ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceLocation Target location Region (and optional availability zone) where the instance is provisioned. Immutable after creation — an instance cannot be moved to another region/zone, which is why location is absent from InstanceUpdateTargetSpec.
---@field name string Name Desired display name of the instance. Mutable: changing it on PUT triggers a rename.
---@field networks? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceTargetSpecNetworksList|distilled.Null Networks Declarative list of network interfaces the instance is attached to. An entry with a subnetId, and an optional id, is a private interface, optionally carrying an ip to pin its fixed address or to associate an existing floating IP; an entry with autoAssignPublicIp alone requests a public (Ext-Net) interface with a platform-assigned public IP; an entry with ip alone attaches a public IP the project already owns, either an additional IP or an Ext-Net IP of the project in the instance's region. See InstanceNetworkRef. The list drives the desired network topology: adding or removing an entry attaches or detaches the corresponding interface on update.
---@field powerState? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstancePowerStateEnum|string|distilled.Null Power state Desired administrative power state of the instance (see PowerStateEnum: ACTIVE, RESCUE, SHELVED, SHUTOFF). Defaults to ACTIVE when omitted. Mutable: changing it on PUT drives the corresponding power transition (start, stop, shelve, rescue).
---@field securityGroups? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceTargetSpecSecurityGroupsList|distilled.Null Security groups Optional list of references to the security groups applied to all of the instance's ports. Each entry carries the security group id. Mutable: changing this list on PUT re-applies the resulting set of security groups to every instance port.
---@field shares? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceTargetSpecSharesList|distilled.Null Shares Declarative list of file storage (shares) attached to the instance, managed exactly like volumes: the diff of this list on PUT drives attach/detach. Attaching a share creates a Manila IP access rule for the instance's interface on the share's network — the instance MUST have an interface on that network or the operation errors. Detaching (removing an entry from this list) deletes the matching access rule and is idempotent. Each entry's accessLevel defaults to READ_WRITE when omitted (see InstanceShareRef).
---@field sshKeyName? string|distilled.Null SSH key name Name of the SSH key pair injected into the instance at boot for initial access. Immutable / create-only: the key is injected once during provisioning and cannot be changed afterward, which is why sshKeyName is absent from InstanceUpdateTargetSpec.
---@field userData? string|distilled.Null User data (cloud-init) Base64-encoded (strict standard encoding) cloud-init payload handed to the instance at boot through the OpenStack metadata service / config drive, and interpreted by cloud-init inside the guest image. The submitted string itself must be at most 65535 bytes once base64-encoded. Write-only: never returned by GET/LIST — deliberately absent from InstanceReadTargetSpec and InstanceCurrentState. Not persisted or stored by the Public Cloud API: the payload is handed to the compute service, which makes it available to the instance via the metadata service; only a non-reversible fingerprint of the value is retained, for change detection. Mutable, but destructively: changing userData on PUT REINSTALLS the instance (a Nova rebuild on the current image), wiping the root disk and all data on it. See InstanceUpdateTargetSpec for the tri-state update semantics.
---@field volumes? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceTargetSpecVolumesList|distilled.Null Volumes Declarative list of block volumes attached to the instance, each referencing a volume by id (see InstanceVolumeRef). Attach/detach is driven by diffing this list on PUT — there is no imperative attach/detach sub-route. Adding a volume reference attaches that volume; removing one detaches it.

---Networks
---
---Declarative list of network interfaces the instance is attached to. An entry with a subnetId, and an optional id, is a private interface, optionally carrying an ip to pin its fixed address or to associate an existing floating IP; an entry with autoAssignPublicIp alone requests a public (Ext-Net) interface with a platform-assigned public IP; an entry with ip alone attaches a public IP the project already owns, either an additional IP or an Ext-Net IP of the project in the instance's region. See InstanceNetworkRef.
---
---The list drives the desired network topology: adding or removing an entry attaches or detaches the corresponding interface on update.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceTargetSpecNetworksList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceNetworkRef[]

---Security groups
---
---Optional list of references to the security groups applied to all of the instance's ports. Each entry carries the security group id.
---
---Mutable: changing this list on PUT re-applies the resulting set of security groups to every instance port.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceTargetSpecSecurityGroupsList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudSecurityGroupSecurityGroupRef[]

---Shares
---
---Declarative list of file storage (shares) attached to the instance, managed exactly like volumes: the diff of this list on PUT drives attach/detach.
---
---Attaching a share creates a Manila IP access rule for the instance's interface on the share's network — the instance MUST have an interface on that network or the operation errors. Detaching (removing an entry from this list) deletes the matching access rule and is idempotent. Each entry's accessLevel defaults to READ_WRITE when omitted (see InstanceShareRef).
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceTargetSpecSharesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceShareRef[]

---Volumes
---
---Declarative list of block volumes attached to the instance, each referencing a volume by id (see InstanceVolumeRef).
---
---Attach/detach is driven by diffing this list on PUT — there is no imperative attach/detach sub-route. Adding a volume reference attaches that volume; removing one detaches it.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceTargetSpecVolumesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceVolumeRef[]

---Desired instance specification (update)
---
---Reduced target specification used on the PUT route, exposing only the fields that can change after creation. Immutable, create-only fields are intentionally absent: location, sshKeyName and the placement group cannot be changed once the instance exists.
---
---Networks, volumes and shares remain declarative: the requested topology is reconciled by diffing these lists against the current attachments.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceUpdateTargetSpec
---@field flavor ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceFlavorRef Flavor Reference to the desired flavor (vCPUs, RAM, local disk). Carries only the flavor id. Mutable: sending a different flavor triggers a resize of the instance.
---@field image? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceImageRef|distilled.Null Image Reference to the desired image. Carries only the image id. Mutable: sending a different image triggers a rebuild of the instance from the new image.
---@field name string Name Desired display name of the instance. Mutable: changing it triggers a rename.
---@field networks? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceUpdateTargetSpecNetworksList|distilled.Null Networks Declarative list of network interfaces the instance is attached to (see InstanceNetworkRef). The list drives the desired network topology: adding or removing an entry attaches or detaches the corresponding interface.
---@field powerState? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstancePowerStateEnum|string|distilled.Null Power state Desired administrative power state (see PowerStateEnum: ACTIVE, RESCUE, SHELVED, SHUTOFF). Defaults to ACTIVE when omitted. Mutable: changing it drives the corresponding power transition (start, stop, shelve, rescue).
---@field securityGroups? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceUpdateTargetSpecSecurityGroupsList|distilled.Null Security groups Optional list of references to the security groups applied to all of the instance's ports. Mutable: changing this list re-applies the resulting set of security groups to every instance port.
---@field shares? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceUpdateTargetSpecSharesList|distilled.Null Shares Declarative list of file storage (shares) attached to the instance, managed exactly like volumes: the diff of this list drives attach/detach. Attaching a share creates a Manila IP access rule for the instance's interface on the share's network — the instance MUST have an interface on that network or the operation errors. Detaching (removing an entry from this list) deletes the matching access rule and is idempotent. Each entry's accessLevel defaults to READ_WRITE when omitted (see InstanceShareRef).
---@field userData? string|distilled.Null User data (cloud-init) Base64-encoded (strict standard encoding) cloud-init payload, at most 65535 bytes once base64-encoded. Write-only: never returned by GET/LIST. Not persisted or stored by the Public Cloud API: the payload is handed to the compute service, which makes it available to the instance via the metadata service on boot/rebuild; only a non-reversible fingerprint of the value is retained, for change detection. Tri-state: omitted or null keeps the current value unchanged; an empty string clears it; a non-empty value replaces it. Destructive: any change (clear or replace) REINSTALLS the instance — a Nova rebuild on the current image — wiping the root disk and all data on it.
---@field volumes? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceUpdateTargetSpecVolumesList|distilled.Null Volumes Declarative list of block volumes attached to the instance (see InstanceVolumeRef). Attach/detach is driven by diffing this list — adding a reference attaches the volume, removing one detaches it. There is no imperative attach/detach sub-route.

