---
---Declarative list of file storage (shares) attached to the instance, managed exactly like volumes: the diff of this list drives attach/detach.
---
---Attaching a share creates a Manila IP access rule for the instance's interface on the share's network — the instance MUST have an interface on that network or the operation errors. Detaching (removing an entry from this list) deletes the matching access rule and is idempotent. Each entry's accessLevel defaults to READ_WRITE when omitted (see InstanceShareRef).
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceUpdateTargetSpecSharesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceShareRef[]

---Volumes
---
---Declarative list of block volumes attached to the instance (see InstanceVolumeRef). Attach/detach is driven by diffing this list — adding a reference attaches the volume, removing one detaches it. There is no imperative attach/detach sub-route.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceUpdateTargetSpecVolumesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceVolumeRef[]

---Instance volume details
---
---Observed block volume attached to an instance, carrying the details reported by the backend. Used in currentState; the creation/update side references a volume by id through InstanceVolumeRef.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceVolume
---@field id? string Unique identifier of the attached volume.
---@field name? string Display name of the attached volume.
---@field size? number Size of the attached volume, in GB.

---Instance volume reference
---
---User-controlled reference to a block volume attached to the instance, used within the declarative volumes list of targetSpec. It carries only the volume id; the full observed volume is exposed in currentState through InstanceVolume.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceVolumeRef
---@field id string Identifier of the volume to attach. Adding this reference attaches the volume; removing it from the volumes list detaches it.

---Instance power state
---
---Power state of an instance as reported by OpenStack Nova, also used to express the desired power state when driving the instance.
---
---Values
---ACTIVE — The instance is running and powered on.
---SHUTOFF — The instance is powered off (stopped) but its resources remain allocated.
---SHELVED — The instance is shelved: it is powered off and its compute resources are released, so it can be unshelved later to resume it.
---RESCUE — The instance is booted in rescue mode from a rescue image.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstancePowerStateEnum "ACTIVE"|"RESCUE"|"SHELVED"|"SHUTOFF"

---Remote console session
---
---A remote console session opened on an instance, returned when creating a console. It provides the connection URL together with the negotiated protocol and display type.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceRemoteConsole
---@field protocol? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceRemoteConsoleProtocolEnum Protocol Protocol of the opened console session (see RemoteConsoleProtocolEnum: VNC, SPICE, SERIAL).
---@field type? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceRemoteConsoleTypeEnum Display type Display type of the opened console session (see RemoteConsoleTypeEnum: NOVNC, XVPVNC, SPICE_HTML5, SERIAL).
---@field url? string Connection URL URL to connect to the remote console. It is short-lived and grants temporary access to the instance's console.

---Remote console protocol
---
---Underlying protocol used to reach an instance's remote console.
---
---Values
---VNC — VNC remote framebuffer protocol, giving graphical access to the instance console.
---SPICE — SPICE remote display protocol, offering richer graphical console access.
---SERIAL — Serial console protocol, giving text-based access to the instance's serial port.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceRemoteConsoleProtocolEnum "SERIAL"|"SPICE"|"VNC"

---Remote console type
---
---Concrete console client/endpoint type returned when requesting access to an instance's remote console, combining a display technology with its transport.
---
---Values
---NOVNC — Browser-based VNC client (noVNC) served over the VNC protocol.
---XVPVNC — Xen VNC Proxy (xvpvnc) console, accessed with a dedicated VNC client.
---SPICE_HTML5 — Browser-based SPICE client (spice-html5) served over the SPICE protocol.
---SERIAL — Serial console exposed over a websocket connection.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceRemoteConsoleTypeEnum "NOVNC"|"SERIAL"|"SPICE_HTML5"|"XVPVNC"

---Instance reservation
---
---A Public Cloud instance reservation: a commitment to a given quantity of instances of a flavor, in a region, for a fixed duration. Once ready, the reservation exposes a dedicated reserved flavor (see currentState.flavor) that instances can be created with to consume the reserved capacity.
---
---The object follows the standard envelope: targetSpec is the desired specification supplied by the user, while currentState reflects what the backend actually provisioned.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceReservationInstanceReservation
---@field checksum? string Checksum Computed hash of the current target specification, used for optimistic concurrency control.
---@field createdAt? string Creation date Timestamp at which the instance reservation was created, in RFC 3339 format.
---@field currentState? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceReservationInstanceReservationCurrentState|distilled.Null Current state Actual state of the instance reservation as reported by the backend, including the reserved flavor to use when creating instances. May be null while the reservation is still being provisioned.
---@field currentTasks? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceReservationInstanceReservationCurrentTasksList|distilled.Null Current tasks Asynchronous operations currently running against this instance reservation. Empty or null when no operation is in progress.
---@field id? string Identifier Unique identifier of the instance reservation.
---@field resourceStatus? ovh.cloud_v2.CommonResourceStatusEnum Resource status Lifecycle status of the instance reservation in the system (for example whether it is being created, ready, or being deleted).
---@field targetSpec? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceReservationInstanceReservationTargetSpec Target specification Desired specification of the instance reservation as supplied by the user (name, location, flavor, quantity and duration). Compare it against currentState to see what the backend actually provisioned.
---@field updatedAt? string Last update date Timestamp of the last update of the instance reservation, in RFC 3339 format.

---Instance reservation current state
---
---Actual state of an instance reservation as observed from the backend.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceReservationInstanceReservationCurrentState
---@field duration? string Duration Commitment period of the reservation, as an ISO 8601 duration (for example P1Y for one year).
---@field endTime? string|distilled.Null End time Date at which the reservation commitment ends (startTime plus duration). Null until the reservation is active.
---@field flavor? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceFlavor Reserved flavor Dedicated flavor created for this reservation. Use its id when creating instances to consume the reserved capacity.
---@field location? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudCommonLocation Current location Region, and availability zone in a 3-AZ region, where the capacity is reserved.
---@field name? string Name Current display name of the instance reservation.
---@field quantity? number Quantity Number of instances of the flavor reserved.
---@field startTime? string|distilled.Null Start time Date at which the reservation commitment starts. Null until the reservation is active.

---Current tasks
---
---Asynchronous operations currently running against this instance reservation. Empty or null when no operation is in progress.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceReservationInstanceReservationCurrentTasksList ovh.cloud_v2.CommonCurrentTask[]

---Desired instance reservation specification
---
---User-controlled specification of an instance reservation: what flavor to reserve, how many instances, where and for how long.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceReservationInstanceReservationTargetSpec
---@field duration string Duration Commitment period of the reservation, as an ISO 8601 duration (for example P1Y for one year).
---@field flavor ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstanceFlavorRef Flavor Reference to the flavor to reserve capacity for.
---@field location ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudCommonLocation Target location Region and, in a 3-AZ region, availability zone where the capacity is reserved. In a 3-AZ region the availability zone is optional: when omitted, the zone with the most stock for the flavor is chosen and returned here. In a region that is not 3-AZ the availability zone is ignored and the reservation is regional. Instances consuming the reservation must be created in this same location.
---@field name string Name Desired display name of the instance reservation.
---@field quantity number Quantity Number of instances of the flavor to reserve.

