---Whether the source-address allowlist of a lakehouse is enforced in its region.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseNetworkAccess
---@field checkedAt? string|distilled.Null Date the region last checked the allowlist. Null when it has not reported it yet.
---@field message? string|distilled.Null Why the allowlist is FAILED or UNSUPPORTED, for people. Null otherwise. It may change; do not parse it.
---@field state? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseNetworkAccessStateEnum DISABLED: no filtering, every address may reach the lakehouse (filtering is off or the list is empty). PENDING: a change of the allowlist is being applied. ENFORCED: only the listed addresses may reach the lakehouse. FAILED: the allowlist could not be applied. UNSUPPORTED: the region no longer enforces allowlists; disable or empty the list.

---Enforcement state of the source-address allowlist of a lakehouse.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseNetworkAccessStateEnum "DISABLED"|"ENFORCED"|"FAILED"|"PENDING"|"UNSUPPORTED"

---What the privileges of a permission apply to: the whole lakehouse, one catalog, or one schema of a catalog.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehousePermissionTarget
---@field catalogId? string|distilled.Null Catalog of a CATALOG or SCHEMA target. Null, or omitted, on a LAKEHOUSE target.
---@field schemaId? string|distilled.Null Schema of a SCHEMA target, which must belong to `catalogId`. Null, or omitted, on any other target.
---@field type ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehousePermissionTargetTypeEnum|string Kind of target. The identifiers must match it, or the request is refused with a 400.

---State of the target of a role permission. ACTIVE: the target exists. TARGET_DELETED: the catalog or schema was deleted, and the permission gives nothing; remove it, or send it back unchanged on update.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehousePermissionTargetStateEnum "ACTIVE"|"TARGET_DELETED"

---Kind of target of a role permission. LAKEHOUSE: every catalog of the lakehouse, including catalogs created later. CATALOG: one catalog and everything in it. SCHEMA: one schema of a catalog, and its tables and views; with SCHEMA targets only, SQL cannot list the schemas of the catalog, so name the schema in your queries. Values may be added.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehousePermissionTargetTypeEnum "CATALOG"|"LAKEHOUSE"|"SCHEMA"

---Stable key of a predefined role. LAKEHOUSE_ADMIN: every data privilege on every catalog; the last Lakehouse Admin assignment cannot be removed. USER_ADMIN: no data privilege, management being granted in OVHcloud IAM. DATA_OWNER: read and change data, create, alter and drop tables and views. DATA_EDITOR: the same, without dropping. DATA_VIEWER: read data and metadata. METADATA_VIEWER: see the names of schemas, tables and views.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehousePredefinedRoleEnum "DATA_EDITOR"|"DATA_OWNER"|"DATA_VIEWER"|"LAKEHOUSE_ADMIN"|"METADATA_VIEWER"|"USER_ADMIN"

---Data privilege of a role permission. BROWSE: see the names of the schemas, tables and views, without their columns. SELECT: read data and metadata. INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE: change data; they come together. ALTER: change the columns, the sort order and the format version of tables. CREATE_TABLE: create tables and views. DROP: drop tables and views. Values may be added.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehousePrivilegeEnum "ALTER"|"BROWSE"|"CREATE_TABLE"|"DELETE"|"DROP"|"INSERT"|"SELECT"|"UPDATE"

