---Load balancer VIP network (observed)
---
---The frontend network the load balancer virtual IP port lives in, as reported by the backend, together with every address through which the VIP is reachable. Unlike the desired specification there is no scalar ip: all addresses, pinned or IPAM-assigned fixed address as well as an associated floating IP, are reported through the addresses list, each carrying its own type.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerLoadbalancerNetwork
---@field addresses? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerLoadbalancerNetworkAddressesList Addresses through which the virtual IP is reachable. Always contains the FIXED address of the VIP port, plus a FLOATING entry when a floating IP is associated with that port.
---@field id? string Identifier of the private network the VIP port lives in.
---@field subnetId? string Identifier of the subnet the VIP port draws its fixed address from.

---Load balancer VIP network address
---
---A single IP address through which the load balancer virtual IP is reachable, with the type telling how that address reaches the VIP port.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerLoadbalancerNetworkAddress
---@field ip? string IP address the virtual IP is reachable at.
---@field type? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerLoadbalancerNetworkAddressTypeEnum Address type How this address reaches the VIP port: FIXED for the address configured on the port itself, FLOATING for a floating IP NAT'd onto it. See LoadbalancerNetworkAddressTypeEnum.

---Load balancer VIP network address type
---
---Nature of an IP address observed on the load balancer virtual IP port, telling how the address reaches the VIP.
---
---Values
---FIXED — The address configured on the VIP port itself, whether assigned by IPAM or pinned at creation.
---FLOATING — A floating IP associated with the VIP port: the address is not configured on the port, the network translates it to the port fixed address.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerLoadbalancerNetworkAddressTypeEnum "FIXED"|"FLOATING"

---Addresses through which the virtual IP is reachable. Always contains the FIXED address of the VIP port, plus a FLOATING entry when a floating IP is associated with that port.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerLoadbalancerNetworkAddressesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerLoadbalancerNetworkAddress[]

---Load balancer VIP network reference (desired)
---
---User-controlled declaration of the load balancer frontend network: the private network and subnet the virtual IP (VIP) port is created in, and therefore the network the listeners are reachable from. subnetId is mandatory. id is optional: when omitted, the network of the subnet is used, and when given, the subnet must belong to it.
---
---The optional IP refines how the VIP is addressed:
---* omitted — the fixed VIP address is assigned by IPAM inside the subnet.
---* an address inside the subnet CIDR — pins the fixed VIP address to that value.
---* an address outside the subnet CIDR — designates an EXISTING floating IP to associate with the VIP port. No address is ever allocated on your behalf.
---
---The VIP network is set at creation and is IMMUTABLE afterwards: it is not part of the update target spec, and neither the network, the subnet, nor the IP can be changed on a load balancer that already exists.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerLoadbalancerNetworkRef
---@field id? string|distilled.Null Network Identifier of the private network the VIP port is created in. This is the load balancer frontend network, from which its listeners are reachable. When omitted, the network of subnetId is used. Immutable after creation.
---@field ip? string|distilled.Null IP address Address of the virtual IP, whose meaning depends on where it falls relative to the subnet CIDR. Inside the subnet CIDR: pins the fixed VIP address instead of letting IPAM assign it; the address must lie in the subnet allocation pool, must not be the subnet gateway address, and must not already be held by another port. Outside the subnet CIDR: designates an EXISTING floating IP of the project to associate with the VIP port — the floating IP is never created for you, must not already be associated with another port, and the subnet must be attached to a router with an external gateway. A public address requires the optional loadbalancer/usePublicIP IAM action. Left unset, the fixed VIP address is assigned by IPAM. Immutable after creation.
---@field subnetId string Subnet Identifier of the subnet the VIP port draws its fixed address from. When id is given, the subnet must belong to that network. Immutable after creation.

