---Desired specification for a private endpoint
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudPrivateEndpointPrivateEndpointTargetSpec
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Private endpoint description
---@field location ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudCommonLocation Target location. Only the region is used, availability zones are not supported
---@field name string Private endpoint name, unique in the project for a given subnet (case-insensitive)
---@field network? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudPrivateEndpointPrivateEndpointNetworkRef|distilled.Null Network to allocate the endpoint port in. Provide one of network or subnet; whichever references are supplied must be mutually consistent (the given subnet must belong to this network) or the request is rejected, and any omitted reference is derived from those given. If network is the only reference, it must have exactly one IPv4 subnet
---@field publicDnsEnabled? boolean|distilled.Null Register the endpoint hostname in the public DNS zone. Defaults to false. Immutable after creation
---@field service ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudPrivateEndpointPrivateEndpointServiceRef Service to expose through the endpoint. A project can have only one private endpoint per service and subnet
---@field subnet? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudPrivateEndpointPrivateEndpointSubnetRef|distilled.Null Subnet to allocate the endpoint port in. Provide one of network or subnet; the subnet must belong to the given network when both are supplied, otherwise the request is rejected. If subnet is the only reference, its parent network is used. Required when vipAddress is set
---@field vipAddress? string|distilled.Null Optional private IP address to assign to the endpoint inside the subnet. It must belong to the subnet CIDR and to one of its allocation pools, must not be the subnet gateway address, and must not already be in use by another port. Setting it requires subnet to be set in the same request. When omitted, an address is picked automatically from the subnet allocation pool. Immutable after creation

