---Instance flavor (catalog entry)
---
---A single compute flavor as advertised by the backend (OpenStack/Nova) for a given region. This is read-only reference data served under /reference: it describes a hardware sizing (vCPUs, RAM, disks) the project can create instances from, not an existing resource.
---
---The catalog is per-region — a flavor returned for one region is not guaranteed to exist, or to carry the same characteristics, in another (see location).
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceInstanceFlavor
---@field bandwidth? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceFlavorBandwidth Bandwidth Network bandwidth an instance of the flavor gets, in Mbit/s.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Description Free-form description of the flavor as reported by the backend. May be null when no description is advertised for this flavor.
---@field disk? number Root disk (GB) Size of the flavor's root disk in GB. This is the primary system disk provisioned for instances created from this flavor.
---@field ephemeral? number Ephemeral disk (GB) Size of the flavor's ephemeral disk in GB. Ephemeral storage is transient — its contents do not survive a rebuild or deletion of the instance. Zero when the flavor provides no ephemeral disk.
---@field gpus? number Number of GPUs Number of physical GPUs provided by the flavor. Zero for flavors without GPU.
---@field id? string Identifier The OpenStack/Nova flavor ID. Stable within a region and used to reference the flavor when creating an instance.
---@field isPublic? boolean Public availability Whether the flavor is publicly available to the project. Private flavors are only visible to the projects they have been explicitly shared with.
---@field location? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudCommonLocation Location Region (and, where applicable, availability zone) where this flavor is offered. The flavor catalog is per-region: a flavor returned for one region is not guaranteed to exist, or to carry the same characteristics, in another.
---@field name? string Name The backend flavor name (for example b2-7, c2-15). This is the commercial/technical name used to identify the sizing in the catalog.
---@field ram? number RAM (MB) Amount of memory provided by the flavor, expressed in MB.
---@field swap? number Swap (MB) Size of the flavor's swap space in MB. Zero when the flavor provides no swap.
---@field vcpus? number vCPUs Number of virtual CPUs provided by the flavor.

---Instance image (catalog entry)
---
---A single OS image as advertised by the backend (OpenStack/Glance) for a given region. This is read-only reference data served under /reference: it describes a bootable image the project can create instances from, not an existing resource.
---
---The image catalog is read-only in APIv2 — there is no create, update or delete on images. The catalog is per-region: an image returned for one region is not guaranteed to exist in another (see location).
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceInstanceImage
---@field createdAt? string Creation date Timestamp at which the image was created on the backend, in RFC 3339 format.
---@field defaultUser? string|distilled.Null Default user Default login user of the image, as set by its publisher, for example almalinux or ubuntu. Null when the image declares none.
---@field id? string Identifier The OpenStack/Glance image ID. Stable within a region and used to reference the image when creating an instance.
---@field location? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudCommonLocation Location Region (and, where applicable, availability zone) where this image is offered. The image catalog is per-region: an image returned for one region is not guaranteed to exist in another.
---@field minDisk? number Minimum disk (GB) Minimum root disk size, in GB, that an instance must provide to boot from this image. A flavor whose disk is smaller than this value cannot be used with the image.
---@field minRam? number Minimum RAM (MB) Minimum amount of memory, in MB, that an instance must provide to boot from this image. A flavor whose RAM is below this value cannot be used with the image.
---@field name? string Name Display name of the image as reported by the backend (for example the distribution and version, such as Debian 12).
---@field osType? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceImageOSTypeEnum Operating system type Operating system family of the image (see ImageOSTypeEnum). Windows images can only boot on Windows flavors.
---@field size? number Size (bytes) Size of the image on the backend, expressed in bytes.
---@field status? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceImageStatusEnum Status Availability status of the image as reported by the backend (see ImageStatusEnum). Only images in an active status can be used to create an instance.
---@field updatedAt? string Last update date Timestamp of the last modification of the image on the backend, in RFC 3339 format.
---@field visibility? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceImageVisibilityEnum Visibility Visibility scope of the image (see ImageVisibilityEnum), for example whether it is a public OVHcloud-provided image or private to the project.

---Service availability (read-only reference data)
---
---Describes where an OVHcloud-operated service can be reached through a private endpoint. The endpoint returns one entry per service, each carrying the connectivity variants it offers with their region, port and transport. This is read-only reference data — it does not reflect existing resources and triggers no OpenStack call.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferencePrivateEndpointServiceAvailability
---@field connectivities? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferencePrivateEndpointServiceAvailabilityConnectivitiesList Enabled connectivity variants of the service
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Service description
---@field name? string Service name

---Enabled connectivity variants of the service
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferencePrivateEndpointServiceAvailabilityConnectivitiesList ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferencePrivateEndpointServiceConnectivity[]

---An enabled connectivity variant of a service reachable through a private endpoint
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferencePrivateEndpointServiceConnectivity
---@field location? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudCommonLocation Location where this connectivity variant is available
---@field name? string Connectivity variant name
---@field port? number Port the service listens on through the endpoint
---@field transport? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudPrivateEndpointServiceTransportEnum Transport protocol of the service

---Product type availability (read-only reference data)
---
---Groups the offerings of a single product type available to a Public Cloud project. The endpoint returns one group per product type. This is read-only reference data computed from the OVHcloud commercial catalog combined with the project's entitlements — it does not reflect existing resources and triggers no OpenStack call.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceProductAvailability
---@field models? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceProductAvailabilityModelsList|distilled.Null Models The offerings of this product type available to the project, each with its per-location availability. Null or empty when no model is available.
---@field type? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceProductTypeEnum Product type The catalog product family this group describes. Currently only instance offerings are emitted.

---Model location availability (read-only reference data)
---
---Describes the availability of a compute model in a single location, including its activation state on the project and current stock status. Read-only reference data.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceProductAvailabilityLocation
---@field availabilityZones? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceProductAvailabilityLocationAvailabilityZonesList|distilled.Null Availability zones The availability zones within the location, for example eu-west-par-a, eu-west-par-b, eu-west-par-c. Empty for single-AZ regions.
---@field enabled? boolean Enabled Whether the location is already activated on the project. When false, the model is available in the location but has not yet been activated for the project.
---@field name? string Location name The region or location identifier, for example GRA11. Identifies the location within a model availability entry.
---@field stockStatus? ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceProductAvailabilityLocationStockStatusMap|distilled.Null Stock status The current stock status of the model in the location, keyed by availability-zone name (for example eu-west-par-a). A 3AZ region has one entry per AZ; single-AZ and localzone regions have a single entry. Present only for the instance product type; absent for every other product type.

---Availability zones
---
---The availability zones within the location, for example eu-west-par-a, eu-west-par-b, eu-west-par-c. Empty for single-AZ regions.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceProductAvailabilityLocationAvailabilityZonesList string[]

---Stock status
---
---The current stock status of the model in the location, keyed by availability-zone name (for example eu-west-par-a). A 3AZ region has one entry per AZ; single-AZ and localzone regions have a single entry. Present only for the instance product type; absent for every other product type.
---@alias ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceProductAvailabilityLocationStockStatusMap { [string]: ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceStockStatusEnum }

---Product model availability (read-only reference data)
---
---Describes a single offering of a product type and the locations where it is available for the project. Read-only reference data.
---@class ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudReferenceProductAvailabilityModel
