---Create a project
---
---Creates a project with a name and a mode. The discovery mode shows the Control Panel in read-only, without a payment method. Creation is asynchronous: follow `resourceStatus` and `currentTasks`.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project`
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudProjectProjectAsync? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project(input) end

---Create an AI agent
---
---Creates an AI agent: a hosted assistant that answers on its own URL, given by `currentState.endpointUrl`, and reached with a token from the `token` action. An agent runs a model with a persona, plus whatever tools, memory and channels its configuration gives it. That configuration can come from a ready-made one published by OVHcloud, from a template of your own, or from settings supplied here — or from none of them, leaving an agent that cannot answer until it is given a model. Parts of it that OVHcloud manages are rejected here; the `globalSettings` preset says which. This is the only point at which this API sets an agent's configuration: from here on the agent holds its own and is configured through its endpoint. Create it paused to finish preparing it before it answers anyone.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/ai/agents/agent`
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectAiAgentAgentRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgent? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_ai_agent_agent(input) end

---Issue a scoped access token for an AI agent
---
---Returns a bearer token to present to the agent at `currentState.endpointUrl`. The token is returned once, here, and is never readable afterwards. Both body fields are optional: send `{}` for the defaults, which are the VIEWER role and the agent's own default lifetime. A lifetime longer than the agent's own maximum is rejected.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/ai/agents/agent/{agentId}/token`
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectAiAgentAgentTokenRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsAgentToken? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_ai_agent_agent_token(input) end

---Create an AI agent template
---
---Registers a reusable configuration that a later agent creation can name through `targetSpec.template.id`. A template stores a configuration; it runs nothing by itself. `targetSpec.name` must be unique within the project's namespace.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/ai/agents/template`
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectAiAgentTemplateRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudAiAgentsTemplate? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_ai_agent_template(input) end

