---Create a lakehouse in your project.
---
---Creates the lakehouse asynchronously. The response is the lakehouse in CREATING, with the creation task in `currentTasks`: follow it on the task routes of the lakehouse, or read the lakehouse until its `resourceStatus` is READY or ERROR.
---
---The lakehouse is created with its first catalog, described by `targetSpec.catalog`. That catalog is then a resource of its own: it is listed under the catalogs of the lakehouse, with its own status and its own creation task, and it is not echoed in the `targetSpec` of the lakehouse. The lakehouse can be READY while its first catalog is still CREATING.
---
---The optional `ipRestrictions` restricts the source addresses allowed to reach the lakehouse (its Apache Iceberg REST catalog, SQL and S3 endpoints) once `ipRestrictionsEnabled` is true. Each entry is a public IPv4 or IPv6 block, or a single address, at most 32 entries with at least one IPv4 block. The list is stored normalized: masked, without duplicates, sorted. Enabling filtering needs a region whose `ipRestrictions` capability is true; otherwise the creation is refused with a 409. The lakehouse turns READY once the region enforces the list, which `currentState.networkAccess` shows.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse`
---Errors: BadRequest, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseLakehouse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse(input) end

---Create a catalog in your lakehouse.
---
---Creates the catalog asynchronously. The response is the catalog in CREATING, with the creation task in `currentTasks`: follow it on the task routes of the catalog, or read the catalog until its `resourceStatus` is READY or ERROR.
---
---The creation is refused with a 409 while the lakehouse is being deleted.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/catalog`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseCatalogRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseCatalog? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse_catalog(input) end

---Create a schema in a catalog of your lakehouse.
---
---Creates the schema asynchronously. The response is the schema in CREATING, with the creation task in `currentTasks`: follow it on the task routes of the schema, or read the schema until its `resourceStatus` is READY or ERROR.
---
---The creation is refused with a 409 while the lakehouse or the catalog is being deleted. A schema cannot be changed after creation.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/catalog/{catalogId}/schema`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseCatalogSchemaRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseSchema? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse_catalog_schema(input) end

---Create a Compute Pool in your lakehouse.
---
---Creates the Compute Pool asynchronously. The response is the Compute Pool in CREATING, with the creation task in `currentTasks`: follow it on the task routes of the Compute Pool, or read the Compute Pool until its `resourceStatus` is READY or ERROR.
---
---A SHARED pool runs your queries on the regional engine; a DEDICATED pool runs them on an engine reserved for the lakehouse, sized by `size`, `minWorkers` and `maxWorkers`. A lakehouse has at most one DEDICATED Compute Pool. The creation is refused with a 409 while the lakehouse is being deleted.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/computePool`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseComputePoolRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseComputePool? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse_compute_pool(input) end

---Create a group in your lakehouse.
---
---Creates the group asynchronously. The response is the group in CREATING, with the creation task in `currentTasks`: follow it on the task routes of the group, or read the group until its `resourceStatus` is READY or ERROR.
---
---The creation is refused with a 409 while the lakehouse is being deleted.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/group`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseGroupRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseGroup? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse_group(input) end

---Add a user to a group of your lakehouse.
---
---Creates the group member asynchronously. The response is the group member in CREATING, with the creation task in `currentTasks`: follow it on the task routes of the group member, or read the group member until its `resourceStatus` is READY or ERROR.
---
---Adding a user to a group gives it every role assigned to the group, so it gives data access. A user is a member of a group at most once. The creation is refused with a 409 while the lakehouse, the group or the user is being deleted, or while a previous membership of the user is still being removed. A member cannot be changed after creation: remove it and add the user again.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/group/{groupId}/member`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseGroupMemberRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseMember? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse_group_member(input) end

---Create a custom role in your lakehouse.
---
---Creates the custom role asynchronously. The response is the role in CREATING, with the creation task in `currentTasks`: follow it on the task routes of the role, or read the role until its `resourceStatus` is READY or ERROR. A role gives nothing until it is assigned: see the role assignment routes.
---
---Each permission gives privileges on one target: the whole lakehouse (every catalog, including catalogs created later), one catalog and everything in it, or one schema of a catalog. A role holds at most 50 permissions, and at most one per target. The privileges of a permission must form a combination the region can enforce: every privilege requires BROWSE; INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE come together and require SELECT and ALTER; ALTER requires SELECT; DROP requires INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE. Any other combination is refused with a 400 that lists the missing privileges.
---
---The name is unique among the roles of the lakehouse, and the names of the predefined roles are reserved. The creation is refused with a 409 while the lakehouse, or a catalog or schema a permission targets, is being deleted.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/role`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseRoleRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseRole? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse_role(input) end

---Assign a role to an identity of your lakehouse.
---
---Creates the role assignment asynchronously. The response is the role assignment in CREATING, with the creation task in `currentTasks`: follow it on the task routes of the role assignment, or read the role assignment until its `resourceStatus` is READY or ERROR.
---
---The identity is a user, a service account or a group of the lakehouse, and `identity.type` must match it, or the creation is refused with a 400. A role assigned to a group applies to every member of the group. Without `scope`, the identity holds the role as it is defined; with a CATALOG scope, it holds the permissions of the role only within that catalog. The predefined roles LAKEHOUSE_ADMIN and USER_ADMIN cover the whole lakehouse and refuse a scope with a 400.
---
---The same role cannot be assigned twice to the same identity with the same scope. The creation is refused with a 409 while the lakehouse, the role, the identity or the scope catalog is being deleted, or while the same role assignment is still being removed. A role assignment cannot be changed after creation: delete it and assign the role again.
---
---Assigning a role gives data access: whoever may call this route can give any role of the lakehouse to any of its identities. Management rights, granted in OVHcloud IAM, are not affected.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/roleAssignment`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.CreatePublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseRoleAssignmentRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseRoleAssignment? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse_role_assignment(input) end

