---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_public_cloud_project_compute_autobackup(input) end

---Get an instance
---
---### Get an instance
---
---Returns a single Public Cloud instance, including its desired `targetSpec` and observed `currentState`.
---
---### Optimistic concurrency
---The `checksum` returned here is the hash of the current `targetSpec`. Keep it and send it back on any subsequent `PUT` or imperative `action` call on the instance to guard against lost updates — it is optional, but omitting it forces the write (see the `PUT` route).
---
---### Filesystem attachments
---`currentState.shares` — the list of filesystems (Manila shares) attached to the instance — is populated **only on this single-instance `GET`**. It is deliberately **not** returned by the `LIST` route for performance reasons; fetch the individual instance when you need it.
---
---`GET /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/compute/instance/{instanceId}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.GetPublicCloudProjectComputeInstanceRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceInstance? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_public_cloud_project_compute_instance(input) end

---Get console output
---
---### Get console output
---
---Returns the **serial console output** (boot / system log) of the instance as text — useful for diagnosing boot problems without opening an interactive console session. This is a **read-only**, synchronous call.
---
---Use the optional `length` query parameter to retrieve only the **last N lines** (the tail) of the log; omit it to return all available output.
---
---`GET /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/compute/instance/{instanceId}/consoleOutput`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.GetPublicCloudProjectComputeInstanceConsoleOutputRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceConsoleOutput? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_public_cloud_project_compute_instance_console_output(input) end

---Get an instance group
---
---### Get an instance group
---
---Returns a single instance group (placement group), including its scheduling `policy` and its members.
---
---### Immutable by design
---Instance groups are **immutable after creation** — there is deliberately **no `PUT` / update route**. Neither the placement `policy` nor the set of members can be changed once the group exists. **Membership is fixed at *instance* creation time**: an instance joins a group via its `targetSpec.group` field when it is created (see the instance `POST`), and cannot be added to or removed from a group afterward. To change grouping you delete and recreate the affected instances into a different group.
---
---`GET /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/compute/instanceGroup/{instanceGroupId}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.GetPublicCloudProjectComputeInstanceGroupRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudInstanceGroupInstanceGroup? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_public_cloud_project_compute_instance_group(input) end

