---List the roles of your lakehouse.
---
---Lists the six predefined roles first, then the custom roles. Every lakehouse holds the six predefined roles from its creation: LAKEHOUSE_ADMIN, USER_ADMIN, DATA_OWNER, DATA_EDITOR, DATA_VIEWER and METADATA_VIEWER. They cannot be changed or deleted, and are not counted in the role quota.
---
---Roles give data access only, through the Apache Iceberg catalog, the SQL engines and the storage of the lakehouse. The calls to this API are authorized by OVHcloud IAM, whatever the roles of the lakehouse.
---
---With its S3 credentials, a user whose roles, its own or its groups', let it read the data of a catalog or schema can also list the object names, sizes and dates of the whole storage of the lakehouse, other catalogs included. It can read or change only the objects of the catalogs and schemas its roles reach.
---
---`GET /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/role`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.ListPublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseRoleRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.ListPublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseRoleResponseBodyList? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse_role(input) end

