---Update a listener
---
---Replaces the listener's target specification as a whole. The body carries the complete desired state of every field `publicCloud.loadbalancer.ListenerPutTargetSpec` exposes, so read the listener first and restate every value you want to keep: a field left out of `targetSpec` is cleared, not carried over from the stored specification.
---
---This matters most for the collection-valued and security-relevant fields. Leaving `allowedCidrs` out clears the allow list and reopens the listener to every source. Leaving `sniContainerRefs` out removes every SNI certificate, and leaving `defaultTlsContainerRef` out removes the default certificate. Leaving `insertHeaders` out stops every header from being inserted, and leaving `tlsVersions` out clears the TLS version restriction. Each of these is replaced as a whole — there is no per-element merge.
---
---The create-only fields `protocol` and `protocolPort` cannot be changed once the listener exists. They are deliberately absent from the update model, and sending one is rejected with a 400.
---
---`name` is required.
---
---The optional `checksum` guards against a lost update: when supplied it must match the listener's current checksum or the request is rejected with a 409 checksum mismatch. Omitting it skips the check and forces the write (last-write-wins).
---
---`PUT /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/loadbalancer/{loadbalancerId}/listener/{listenerId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.PutPublicCloudProjectLoadbalancerListenerRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerListener? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:put_public_cloud_project_loadbalancer_listener(input) end

---Update an L7 policy
---
---Replaces the L7 policy's target specification as a whole, including its action and evaluation position.
---
---`PUT /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/loadbalancer/{loadbalancerId}/listener/{listenerId}/l7policy/{l7PolicyId}`
---Errors: NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.PutPublicCloudProjectLoadbalancerListenerL7policyRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerL7Policy? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:put_public_cloud_project_loadbalancer_listener_l7_policy(input) end

---Update a pool
---
---Replaces the pool's target specification as a whole. The body carries the complete desired state of every field `publicCloud.loadbalancer.PoolUpdateTargetSpec` exposes — `algorithm`, `description`, `healthMonitor`, `name` and `persistence` — so read the pool first and restate every value you want to keep: a field left out of `targetSpec` is cleared, not carried over from the stored specification. Leaving `healthMonitor` out deletes the pool's health monitor, and leaving `persistence` out disables session persistence.
---
---The create-only field `protocol` cannot be changed once the pool exists. It is deliberately absent from the update model, and sending it is rejected with a 400.
---
---`algorithm` is required. When a `healthMonitor` is sent, it is itself a complete specification: `type`, `delay`, `timeout` and `maxRetries` are all required — mirroring the create route — and every optional monitor field left out is cleared. The monitor `type` is immutable once the monitor exists, so restate the current type.
---
---The optional `checksum` guards against a lost update: when supplied it must match the pool's current checksum or the request is rejected with a 409 checksum mismatch. Omitting it skips the check and forces the write (last-write-wins).
---
---`PUT /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/loadbalancer/{loadbalancerId}/pool/{poolId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.PutPublicCloudProjectLoadbalancerPoolRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLoadbalancerPool? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:put_public_cloud_project_loadbalancer_pool(input) end

---Update a pool member
---
---Replaces the member's target specification as a whole. The body carries the complete desired state of every field `publicCloud.loadbalancer.MemberUpdateTargetSpec` exposes — `backup`, `monitor`, `name` and `weight` — so read the member first and restate every value you want to keep: a field left out of `targetSpec` is cleared, not carried over from the stored specification.
---
---`monitor` is replaced as a whole, and so are the fields inside it. Leaving `monitor` out clears the health-monitoring override, and health monitoring falls back to the member's own address and protocol port. Sending a `monitor` that omits `address` or `port` clears just that one, and the member's own value is used for it.
---
---The create-only fields `address`, `protocolPort` and `subnet` cannot be changed once the member exists. They are deliberately absent from the update model, and sending one is rejected with a 400.
---
---The optional `checksum` guards against a lost update: when supplied it must match the member's current checksum or the request is rejected with a 409 checksum mismatch. Omitting it skips the check and forces the write (last-write-wins).
---
---`PUT /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/loadbalancer/{loadbalancerId}/pool/{poolId}/member/{memberId}`
