---Update a lakehouse of your project.
---
---Replaces the lakehouse's target specification as a whole. The body carries the complete desired state of every field `publicCloud.lakehouse.LakehouseUpdateTargetSpec` exposes — `description`, `ipRestrictions`, `ipRestrictionsEnabled` and `name` — so read the lakehouse first and restate every value you want to keep: a field left out of `targetSpec` is cleared, not carried over from the stored specification. `ipRestrictions` and `ipRestrictionsEnabled` are required, so that a client unaware of them cannot wipe the allowlist by leaving them out: send the current list and switch to keep them.
---
---The create-only fields `catalog` and `region` cannot be changed once the lakehouse exists. They are deliberately absent from the update model, and sending one is rejected with a 400.
---
---A change of `ipRestrictions` or `ipRestrictionsEnabled` is applied asynchronously, since the region must enforce it: the response is 202 with the lakehouse UPDATING and the new task in `currentTasks`, and the lakehouse turns READY once `currentState.networkAccess` reads ENFORCED (or DISABLED). The list is validated as on creation; `ipRestrictionsEnabled` true with an empty list is rejected with a 400. Turning filtering off keeps the entries. Enabling filtering or adding addresses needs a region whose `ipRestrictions` capability is true, otherwise it is refused with a 409; disabling filtering or removing entries is always accepted.
---
---On a READY lakehouse a change of `name` or `description` alone is applied at once: the response is 200 with the lakehouse READY. On a lakehouse in ERROR the change is applied asynchronously, even when the specification is unchanged, to bring the lakehouse out of ERROR: the response is 202 with the lakehouse UPDATING and the new task in `currentTasks`. The update is refused with a 409 while the lakehouse is CREATING, UPDATING or DELETING, and after a refused deletion, from which only a new deletion is accepted.
---
---The optional `checksum` guards against a lost update: when supplied it must match the lakehouse's current checksum or the request is rejected with a 409 checksum mismatch. Omitting it skips the check and forces the write (last-write-wins).
---
---`PUT /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.PutPublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseLakehouse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:put_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse(input) end

