---The create-only field `name` cannot be changed once the catalog exists. It is deliberately absent from the update model, and sending it is rejected with a 400.
---
---On a READY catalog the change is applied at once: the response is 200 with the catalog READY. On a catalog in ERROR the change is applied asynchronously, even when the specification is unchanged, to bring the catalog out of ERROR: the response is 202 with the catalog UPDATING and the new task in `currentTasks`. The update is refused with a 409 while the catalog is CREATING, UPDATING or DELETING, and after a refused deletion, from which only a new deletion is accepted.
---
---The optional `checksum` guards against a lost update: when supplied it must match the catalog's current checksum or the request is rejected with a 409 checksum mismatch. Omitting it skips the check and forces the write (last-write-wins).
---
---`PUT /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/catalog/{catalogId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
