---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:put_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse_catalog(input) end

---Update a Compute Pool of your lakehouse.
---
---Replaces the Compute Pool's target specification as a whole. The body carries the complete desired state of every field `publicCloud.lakehouse.ComputePoolUpdateTargetSpec` exposes — `description`, `idleSuspendMinutes`, `maxWorkers`, `minWorkers`, `size` and `tier` — so read the Compute Pool first and restate every value you want to keep: a field left out of `targetSpec` is cleared, not carried over from the stored specification. For a DEDICATED pool, a shape field left out is reset to its default: `size` XS, `minWorkers` 1, `maxWorkers` equal to `minWorkers`, `idleSuspendMinutes` 15.
---
---The create-only field `name` cannot be changed once the Compute Pool exists. It is deliberately absent from the update model, and sending it is rejected with a 400.
---
---When only `description` changes on a READY pool, the change is applied at once: the response is 200 with the pool READY. When `tier` or the resolved shape changes, or when the pool is in ERROR, the change is applied asynchronously: the response is 202 with the pool UPDATING and the new task in `currentTasks`. The update is refused with a 409 while a task of the pool is in progress or the pool is DELETING. A lakehouse has at most one DEDICATED Compute Pool.
---
---The optional `checksum` guards against a lost update: when supplied it must match the Compute Pool's current checksum or the request is rejected with a 409 checksum mismatch. Omitting it skips the check and forces the write (last-write-wins).
---
---`PUT /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/computePool/{computePoolId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.PutPublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseComputePoolRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudLakehouseComputePool? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:put_public_cloud_project_managed_analytics_lakehouse_compute_pool(input) end

