---Update a custom role of your lakehouse.
---
---Replaces the role's target specification as a whole. The body carries the complete desired state of every field `publicCloud.lakehouse.RoleUpdateTargetSpec` exposes — `description` and `permissions` — so read the role first and restate every value you want to keep: a field left out of `targetSpec` is cleared, and `permissions` replaces the whole list of permissions, it is not merged with it. The permissions follow the rules of the creation.
---
---The create-only field `name` cannot be changed once the role exists. It is deliberately absent from the update model, and sending it is rejected with a 400. A predefined role cannot be changed: the update is refused with a 409.
---
---A permission whose catalog or schema was deleted (`targetState` TARGET_DELETED) can be sent back unchanged, so a body built from a read always succeeds; a new permission on a deleted catalog or schema is refused with a 404.
---
---When only the description changes, or when the role has no role assignment, the change is applied at once: the response is 200 with the role READY. When the permissions of an assigned role change, or when the role is in ERROR, the change is applied asynchronously: the response is 202 with the role UPDATING and the new task in `currentTasks`. The update is refused with a 409 while the role is CREATING, UPDATING or DELETING.
---
---The optional `checksum` guards against a lost update: when supplied it must match the role's current checksum or the request is rejected with a 409 checksum mismatch. Omitting it skips the check and forces the write (last-write-wins).
---
---`PUT /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/role/{roleId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.PutPublicCloudProjectManagedAnalyticsLakehouseRoleRequest
