---Update a volume
---
---Replaces the volume's target specification as a whole. The body carries the complete desired state of every field `publicCloud.blockStorage.BlockUpdateTargetSpec` exposes (`name`, `size` and `volumeType`), so read the volume first and restate every value you want to keep: a field left out of `targetSpec` is cleared, not carried over from the stored specification.
---
---The create-only fields `location`, `encryption` and `createFrom` cannot be changed once the volume exists. They are deliberately absent from the update model, and sending one is rejected with a 400.
---
---`name` and `size` are both required. `size` can only grow: restate the volume's current size to keep it, or send a larger value to extend it, because shrinking a volume is not supported. Leaving `size` out, or sending 0, is rejected with a 400. Restate `volumeType` to keep it; sending a different type triggers an online retype (migration).
---
---The optional `checksum` guards against a lost update: when supplied it must match the volume's current checksum or the request is rejected with a 409 checksum mismatch. Omitting it skips the check and forces the write (last-write-wins).
---
---`PUT /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/storage/block/volume/{id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.PutPublicCloudProjectStorageBlockVolumeRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudBlockStorageBlock? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:put_public_cloud_project_storage_block_volume(input) end

---Update a file storage
---
---Replaces the file storage's target specification as a whole. The body carries the complete desired state of every field `publicCloud.storage.file.FileStorageUpdateTargetSpec` exposes (`description`, `name` and `size`), so read the file storage first and restate every value you want to keep: a field left out of `targetSpec` is cleared, not carried over from the stored specification. Leaving `description` out clears the description.
---
---The create-only fields `protocol`, `shareType`, `shareNetwork`, `location`, `encryption` and `createFrom` cannot be changed once the file storage exists. They are deliberately absent from the update model, and sending one is rejected with a 400.
---
---`name` and `size` are both required. `size` can only grow: restate the current size to keep it, or send a larger value to extend the file storage, because shrinking one is not supported.
---
---The optional `checksum` guards against a lost update: when supplied it must match the file storage's current checksum or the request is rejected with a 409 checksum mismatch. Omitting it skips the check and forces the write (last-write-wins).
---
---`PUT /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/storage/file/share/{fileStorageId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input ovh.cloud_v2.PutPublicCloudProjectStorageFileShareRequest
---@return ovh.cloud_v2.PublicCloudStorageFileFileStorage? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:put_public_cloud_project_storage_file_share(input) end

