---Reset the credentials of a user of your lakehouse and get the new ones.
---
---Generates new credentials for the user and returns them once, in this response: the client secret and the S3 secret key cannot be read again, so store them safely. The previous credentials stop working.
---
---The user must be READY: the reset is refused with a 409 otherwise. The reset is synchronous: it changes neither the target specification, nor the checksum, nor the status of the user, and records no task.
---
---`POST /publicCloud/project/{projectId}/managedAnalytics/lakehouse/{lakehouseId}/user/{userId}/credentials/reset`
